1
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:12,780
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

2
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:30,770
Mnet original dance series.

3
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,970
Street World Fighter: Directors' War.

4
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:39,040
Here, ten choreographers have gathered...

5
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:41,550
to prove themselves as directors.

6
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:44,920
The choreographers have engraved their signature moves...

7
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:46,650
into people's minds...

8
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:47,750
through countless choreography and performances.

9
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:49,720
They will now throw themselves into the performance directing war,

10
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:51,060
where they'll go beyond competing with choreography...

11
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:53,360
and prove themselves with their production of art.

12
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,660
Directing and making choreography are different.

13
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:56,660
Your name being credited as a director...

14
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:58,100
is a whole different thing.

15
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,360
I must get my name on it no matter what.

16
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,500
They'll fight with their brains, not their bodies.

17
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:02,870
My brain is about to explode.

18
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:04,870
They'll fight solo, not as a crew.

19
00:01:04,870 --> 00:01:06,400
The war to put their name...

20
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,140
on the credit as a director...

21
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:10,070
will start.

22
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:13,550
Every choreographer's dream is to be credited as a director.

23
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:15,150
I came to fight as a director.

24
00:01:15,150 --> 00:01:16,980
If I lose, I'll retire.

25
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:19,480
Really? I'm the first to get eliminated?

26
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:22,450
The real battle of directors...

27
00:01:22,450 --> 00:01:23,960
starts here at the Directors' Lab.

28
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:25,890
It's so pretty.

29
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:26,960
I can't close my mouth.

30
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,660
It feels like a dream.

31
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:30,300
In the Directors' Lab,

32
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:32,800
there are ten Directors' Rooms,

33
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,300
one for each director.

34
00:01:35,630 --> 00:01:37,840
In the Directors' Room, their strategies...

35
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:39,440
- and responsibilities will clash. - This is hard.

36
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,970
My brain is fully active for 24 hours.

37
00:01:40,970 --> 00:01:42,940
You need to plan smartly.

38
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:44,510
Sometimes, they'll persuade the others.

39
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:45,680
Nobody would've thought about it.

40
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:46,910
I'll pick first.

41
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:48,710
Maybe I shouldn't have let him go first.

42
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:50,550
You need to find the winning team.

43
00:01:50,550 --> 00:01:51,550
It doesn't matter if I get eliminated.

44
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:53,590
If you want to win, take me.

45
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:54,590
It was ridiculous.

46
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:56,320
He was the least persuasive.

47
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,120
Sometimes, they need to keep their competitors in check.

48
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:59,220
Stabbed me in the back?

49
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:00,590
You can't trust anyone.

50
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:01,730
Isn't it ridiculous?

51
00:02:01,730 --> 00:02:03,190
It's the space of responsibility...

52
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:05,800
where they must face their decisions until the end.

53
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,470
How could I lose?

54
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:09,370
Can you turn off the lights, please?

55
00:02:09,370 --> 00:02:10,840
I want to quit.

56
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,440
This could be my last round.

57
00:02:14,270 --> 00:02:15,910
The most important weapon...

58
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:18,680
for the ten choreographers to get their names...

59
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,680
on the credit board is...

60
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,280
the dancers.

61
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:28,590
In Directors' War, the dancers could become...

62
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:29,590
the choreographers' weapons.

63
00:02:29,590 --> 00:02:31,290
They're fully armed with all sorts of weapons.

64
00:02:31,290 --> 00:02:32,590
There's no way I can lose.

65
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,360
Yes!
Or they could become a trap.

66
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:36,900
How can you get it wrong?

67
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,430
We only practiced for 15 minutes.

68
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:40,060
The choreography is too difficult.

69
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:41,500
I don't think we can learn it.

70
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:42,970
It's such a big risk.

71
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:44,500
But why?

72
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,500
You're not a professional.

73
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:46,770
Why do you start late?

74
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:48,070
Is it too far to run?

75
00:02:48,070 --> 00:02:49,140
You can do it, so why won't you?

76
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:50,140
What do you think?

77
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:51,580
Am I wrong?

78
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:52,910
They either keep you alive...

79
00:02:52,910 --> 00:02:54,080
or make you break down.

80
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:56,950
I must not have tried hard enough.

81
00:02:56,950 --> 00:02:58,920
I should've worked harder.

82
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:04,820
As the leader, these dancers are relying on me.

83
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:05,820
I'm sorry.

84
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:07,060
If we meet again next time,

85
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:08,430
I'll make sure you win.

86
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:10,160
You need to bear the responsibilities.

87
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,900
That shows your capabilities as a director.

88
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,700
The number of dancers is 400.

89
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:14,800
There's no end to them.

90
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,800
This is fun.

91
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:16,900
This is huge!

92
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:17,900
We're dancers.

93
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,970
It's the Class Mission, director version.

94
00:03:19,970 --> 00:03:22,110
We have Vata, who'll play the role of BADA.

95
00:03:22,110 --> 00:03:23,840
Imagine I'm a director...

96
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,540
and think about how to place them.

97
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:28,310
Has anyone here directed more solo artists than me?

98
00:03:28,310 --> 00:03:29,980
- The dancers who'll work... - You've got to be kidding me.

99
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:31,050
- with the directors... - I got chills.

100
00:03:31,050 --> 00:03:32,850
- Global kid dancers. - Global kid dancers.

101
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:34,390
Direct me!

102
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:36,890
- Kid dancers? - I didn't see this coming at all.

103
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:37,960
My gosh.

104
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:38,960
He's 11.
For real?

105
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,090
He's insane.

106
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:45,000
Some will remain as choreographers,

107
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,570
and some will be promoted as directors.

108
00:03:47,570 --> 00:03:48,570
I must win...

109
00:03:48,570 --> 00:03:49,670
if I want to avoid the Last Stage.

110
00:03:49,670 --> 00:03:51,770
I could never do the Last Stage.

111
00:03:51,770 --> 00:03:53,070
That's a nightmare.

112
00:03:53,070 --> 00:03:54,440
Within 24 hours,

113
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:55,840
you need to prove yourself.

114
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,910
It's an impromptu direction battle.

115
00:03:57,910 --> 00:03:58,980
Are they crazy?

116
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:00,110
Twenty-four hours is impossible.

117
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:01,180
Is this really happening?

118
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:03,250
A choreographer will be eliminated.

119
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:04,720
Can I advance?

120
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:05,850
I really can't do this.

121
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:07,220
This is really the end.

122
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:08,450
I wish I was dreaming.

123
00:04:08,450 --> 00:04:10,220
Only one person will transcend...

124
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:13,090
being a choreographer and become the director.

125
00:04:13,090 --> 00:04:14,090
My goal is to win.

126
00:04:14,090 --> 00:04:15,630
I'll engrave my name on it.

127
00:04:16,030 --> 00:04:18,930
Who will become the one choreographer...

128
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:22,170
that will mark their name as a director?

129
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,570
The winning director will get the right to direct...

130
00:04:23,570 --> 00:04:25,900
the opening stage of a global awards show,

131
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:27,210
directing grant,

132
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:29,470
and a refresh trip...

133
00:04:29,470 --> 00:04:32,910
to recharge themselves after the fierce battle.

134
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:34,580
World-class choreographers'...

135
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:37,450
unprecedented credit war starts.

136
00:04:37,450 --> 00:04:39,220
I don't think I can lose to anyone.

137
00:04:39,950 --> 00:04:40,950
Ready,

138
00:04:42,690 --> 00:04:43,690
fight.

139
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:46,760
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

140
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:48,290
("Royalty" performed by Yoon Mi Rae and Tiger JK)

141
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:59,800
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

142
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:07,880
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

143
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:21,730
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

144
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:22,760
Okay.

145
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:24,360
It's important to show your energy.

146
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,830
When I want to show my energy, I wear gloves.

147
00:05:29,770 --> 00:05:31,940
Nobody can beat my ribbon energy.

148
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:35,440
It's different from "Street Woman Fighter" I know of.

149
00:05:36,070 --> 00:05:37,110
Simeez...

150
00:05:37,110 --> 00:05:38,840
is back with light pink.

151
00:05:39,110 --> 00:05:40,110
(Queen is back.)

152
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:41,850
It's so pretty.

153
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:42,980
No!

154
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:44,320
I hate this!

155
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:46,080
I need to put this on again? Okay.

156
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:47,520
I do feel a bit pressured.

157
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:49,590
I was always with the members of La Chica...

158
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:51,020
on the pink chair.

159
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:52,560
But I'm here on my own.

160
00:05:52,590 --> 00:05:54,230
Forget about Simeez who was the youngest member.

161
00:05:54,230 --> 00:05:56,990
I'm already reborn as the golden director.

162
00:05:57,230 --> 00:05:59,700
I'm working as a choreographer and a director.

163
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:02,100
My specialty as a choreographer is heels dance.

164
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,370
I made the heels myself. Cute, right?

165
00:06:04,370 --> 00:06:07,070
Nowadays, I'm working as IVE's performance director.

166
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:10,710
Lollapalooza, award shows, concerts,

167
00:06:10,710 --> 00:06:12,240
and the overall performance.

168
00:06:12,410 --> 00:06:14,050
I'm good at making conceptual stages.

169
00:06:14,610 --> 00:06:17,080
A performance director isn't a choreography director.

170
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:19,450
Deciding a concept, stage directing,

171
00:06:19,450 --> 00:06:21,850
stage designing, dancer arrangements, and lighting.

172
00:06:21,850 --> 00:06:23,390
You oversee everything.

173
00:06:23,490 --> 00:06:25,190
You can't have a directors' war without me.

174
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:26,590
I've sharpened my claws for five years.

175
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:28,030
I'll show them.

176
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:29,860
I'm making my entry.

177
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:31,860
I've walked in myself.

178
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,200
"Directors' Square? Directors' Room?"

179
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:36,070
(A grand entrance)

180
00:06:36,070 --> 00:06:37,100
My gosh!

181
00:06:37,670 --> 00:06:39,470
It's so pretty.

182
00:06:41,170 --> 00:06:43,040
Gosh, okay.

183
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:46,510
This is better than my house.

184
00:06:46,510 --> 00:06:47,750
There were ten rooms...

185
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:50,380
with each director's unique signature color.

186
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,380
We have separate spaces.

187
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:54,390
You can have meetings and talk.

188
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:58,790
They made it look like a studio to match the director concept.

189
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,830
We need to plan out the formations and concepts.

190
00:07:02,190 --> 00:07:06,260
The first thing you do as a director...

191
00:07:06,430 --> 00:07:07,970
is buying a laptop and a tablet.

192
00:07:07,970 --> 00:07:09,200
You need to draw a lot...

193
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:12,200
and monitor performances on a big screen.

194
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:16,340
A board makes it easy to see the formation.

195
00:07:16,470 --> 00:07:19,640
I write down ideas and develop them like I write a diary.

196
00:07:19,810 --> 00:07:21,950
Directors are all about brains.

197
00:07:21,950 --> 00:07:23,480
My brain is about to explode.

198
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,380
Do you not see my hair falling?

199
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,750
No, this...

200
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:27,750
(Sighing)

201
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:29,490
(Screaming)

202
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:31,360
What should I do with this?

203
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:33,360
Simeez.

204
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:35,160
My gosh.

205
00:07:36,130 --> 00:07:38,100
You can see everything.

206
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:40,500
We'd be keeping each other in check.

207
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:43,630
(Getting ready)

208
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,100
I'll make one round.

209
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,470
I need to see.

210
00:07:46,940 --> 00:07:48,010
Yellow.

211
00:07:48,010 --> 00:07:49,110
JEONG MIN JUN.

212
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:50,440
Okay, Renan.

213
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:52,810
All the prominent choreographers and directors have joined,

214
00:07:52,810 --> 00:07:54,210
which made me feel intimidated.

215
00:07:55,410 --> 00:07:56,750
Let's see who'll join.

216
00:07:57,010 --> 00:07:58,680
It's BADA.

217
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,080
Koo Young is joining?

218
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,420
I expected INGYOO.

219
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:02,790
NaiN...

220
00:08:02,790 --> 00:08:04,320
It'll be a good chance for her to gain a lot of experience.

221
00:08:04,390 --> 00:08:06,460
It's my chance to climb higher.

222
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:07,890
If I'm dancing myself,

223
00:08:07,890 --> 00:08:09,390
I can definitely win.

224
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:10,930
But this isn't "Street Woman Fighter."

225
00:08:10,930 --> 00:08:13,000
BADA is more of a dancer.

226
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:15,530
I won't lose in terms of mega crew performance.

227
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,970
I don't know if she'll be able to do the missions...

228
00:08:16,970 --> 00:08:18,340
other than the mega crew performance.

229
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:19,600
Kasper...

230
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:22,740
I think he's a bit slow to catch up to the trend.

231
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:24,540
They'll be beneath me.

232
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:26,310
Who's that?

233
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:28,150
Who is it? JEONG MIN JUN?

234
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:29,650
I haven't heard of him.

235
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:31,480
There are so many things I can show.

236
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,780
I'm definitely confident.

237
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:34,720
We'll be fighting using our skills.

238
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,650
We'll found out.

239
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:40,630
I'm finally here. Let's do this.

240
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:44,160
(The second choreographer full of nerves enters.)

241
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:46,260
"Street World Fighter: Directors' War."

242
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:47,970
Someone's here.

243
00:08:48,670 --> 00:08:50,070
(He exhales in awe...)

244
00:08:50,070 --> 00:08:52,700
(and inhales in shock.)

245
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:53,840
It's BABYZOO.

246
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:55,770
BABYZOO came.

247
00:08:55,770 --> 00:08:58,480
He's a prominent choreographer...

248
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,910
with unique experiences.

249
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,610
Hello, I'm BABYZOO, a choreographer.

250
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:05,150
I was a battler,

251
00:09:05,150 --> 00:09:07,250
so I'm exceptionally competitive.

252
00:09:07,850 --> 00:09:09,320
My specialty is waacking.

253
00:09:09,690 --> 00:09:12,790
I went to a dance battle almost once every week.

254
00:09:13,460 --> 00:09:15,560
He's one of the most experienced battlers in Korea.

255
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,560
(Yoon Ji)

256
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:20,260
I placed 1st and 2nd countless times.

257
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:21,670
I take pride in it.

258
00:09:21,930 --> 00:09:23,870
I thought he was only good at dance battles.

259
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:25,770
He's stealing our jobs.

260
00:09:26,670 --> 00:09:28,040
Making use of my specialty,

261
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:30,170
I make many signature moves with my hands.

262
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,110
Dynamic and powerful.

263
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:35,810
Girl groups, boy groups, and co-ed groups.

264
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:37,950
I do a variety of things.

265
00:09:37,950 --> 00:09:41,650
He's improved even more since he worked with ALLDAY PROJECT.

266
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:44,160
He only started directing recently.

267
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:45,290
He's a rookie.

268
00:09:45,290 --> 00:09:46,890
I'll call myself a super rookie.

269
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,490
Given his personality,

270
00:09:48,490 --> 00:09:49,730
he wouldn't join if he wasn't aiming to win.

271
00:09:49,730 --> 00:09:50,730
Yes, I want to win.

272
00:09:50,730 --> 00:09:52,830
I'm very confident. I want to show everything.

273
00:09:52,830 --> 00:09:54,470
I want everyone to be wary of me.

274
00:09:54,470 --> 00:09:56,770
He's still like a junior.

275
00:09:57,130 --> 00:09:58,140
Lack of experience?

276
00:09:58,140 --> 00:10:00,400
I'm not exactly wary of him.

277
00:10:00,470 --> 00:10:02,440
Is there anyone...

278
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:03,940
you're wary of?

279
00:10:04,610 --> 00:10:05,840
Who I'm wary of?

280
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:09,050
Simeez has directed...

281
00:10:09,050 --> 00:10:12,380
very feminine artists.

282
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:16,490
Will she be able to direct male artists?

283
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:18,860
I could beat her in that regard.

284
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:21,890
Everyone is my competitor,

285
00:10:21,890 --> 00:10:23,390
but especially...

286
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:24,430
NaiN?

287
00:10:24,430 --> 00:10:26,600
- NaiN. - I'm wary of her.

288
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:30,000
Because we kept working on the same projects recently.

289
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,340
(The choreographer who makes the super rookie become wary of)

290
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:33,570
Hello. I'm NaiN, a choreographer.

291
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:36,070
(The leader of TURNS, NaiN)

292
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:38,440
(TURNS won "Street Dance Girls Fighter.")

293
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,540
It gave me the boost...

294
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:42,480
to grow a lot faster than others.

295
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:45,550
I have the most experience among those my age.

296
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:47,420
She's good at hip concepts.

297
00:10:47,420 --> 00:10:48,720
She can do powerful moves too.

298
00:10:48,790 --> 00:10:50,390
She makes feminine choreography too.

299
00:10:50,390 --> 00:10:51,720
She's good at everything cheeky.

300
00:10:52,090 --> 00:10:53,790
I can choreograph differently for different songs.

301
00:10:53,990 --> 00:10:55,830
Her best output is "Golden."

302
00:10:55,830 --> 00:10:58,160
She shook up the whole K-pop choreography industry.

303
00:10:58,260 --> 00:11:00,930
I directed Macy's in the USA.

304
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:04,240
Switching between performances and K-pop choreography.

305
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,700
She's a rising young director.

306
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:08,770
I'm in charge of Hearts2Hearts.

307
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:12,810
Experience and age aren't always proportional to skills.

308
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,450
I'll show you.

309
00:11:14,710 --> 00:11:16,150
Hold on. What's this?

310
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:18,050
It's NaiN.

311
00:11:18,180 --> 00:11:19,350
Who's here?

312
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:22,890
Jo Na In, my rival, has arrived.

313
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:24,920
- Let's do this. - As a friendly rival,

314
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,320
I'm preparing myself thoroughly.

315
00:11:27,830 --> 00:11:28,960
NaiN.

316
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,390
Why are you here?

317
00:11:30,390 --> 00:11:32,600
Our projects overlapped so much.

318
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:35,400
It was always NaiN and BABYZOO or BABYZOO and NaiN.

319
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,770
If I'd worked on ALLDAY PROJECT, I would've done better.

320
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:40,340
- Why are you here? - I feel awkward.

321
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:41,810
- Why are you here? - I can't do this.

322
00:11:41,810 --> 00:11:43,210
- Go home now. - I really can't do this.

323
00:11:43,210 --> 00:11:46,280
I'll use this chance to beat him once and for all.

324
00:11:46,310 --> 00:11:48,410
- You're so... - I'll definitely win.

325
00:11:48,410 --> 00:11:50,310
As I expected, NaiN and BABYZOO...

326
00:11:50,310 --> 00:11:52,180
are all geared up.

327
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:55,620
Seeing them here is nice,

328
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:56,690
but I hate it at the same time.

329
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,660
"The director who'll lead the generational change..."

330
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:00,830
"is me."

331
00:12:00,930 --> 00:12:04,360
This is important. "I'm scared."

332
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:07,530
Is there anyone you didn't want to meet on the show?

333
00:12:07,530 --> 00:12:08,900
(Thinking)

334
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:10,470
INGYOO.

335
00:12:10,570 --> 00:12:12,170
He left a very strong impression with how tough he talks...

336
00:12:12,170 --> 00:12:13,170
on "Street Man Fighter,"

337
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:14,370
so I was scared.

338
00:12:14,870 --> 00:12:18,140
("Street Man Fighter's" official villain)

339
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:20,380
He is scary, and so is his dancing.

340
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:25,420
Nobody welcomes me

341
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:26,620
Oh, yes.

342
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,920
Directors' War, what will my fate be like?

343
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:31,120
I'm INGYOO, a choreographer.

344
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,790
I lead WE DEM BOYZ.

345
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:36,230
They're the first dance crew any artist would go to.

346
00:12:36,290 --> 00:12:38,830
INGYOO is the trendiest dancer.

347
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,800
The heart of WE DEM BOYZ is INGYOO.

348
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:42,500
He has insane skills.

349
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:43,500
NCT...

350
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:44,670
RIIZE...

351
00:12:44,670 --> 00:12:47,000
He's optimized for boy groups.

352
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:48,970
When I think about Jennie,

353
00:12:48,970 --> 00:12:50,640
all I can think of is INGYOO.

354
00:12:50,710 --> 00:12:51,910
(The choreographer of "like JENNIE")

355
00:12:51,910 --> 00:12:54,380
I have good achievements as a choreographer.

356
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:56,750
INGYOO is a really good director.

357
00:12:56,810 --> 00:12:57,820
Let's go!

358
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:59,780
Last year-end awards show. Was it MMA?

359
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:01,620
It was so cool.

360
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:03,790
Golden Disc Awards. It was sensational.

361
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:06,420
He's established himself as a director.

362
00:13:06,590 --> 00:13:08,390
It looks like a piece of painting,

363
00:13:08,530 --> 00:13:09,930
and you see the amazing dance next.

364
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:13,200
It worked out. It was rewarding for sure.

365
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:16,200
I have good sense and gut feelings, so I'm confident.

366
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:18,140
I can assure you...

367
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:21,170
that the others here would want to get directed by me.

368
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:22,770
Everyone!

369
00:13:22,910 --> 00:13:25,140
Let's have fun!

370
00:13:25,810 --> 00:13:26,880
But...

371
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:28,310
No matter who choreographed it,

372
00:13:28,310 --> 00:13:31,320
"like JENNIE" would've been a hit, you know.

373
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,480
He's lucky.

374
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,560
The rooms are transparent.

375
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,760
(Glancing)

376
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:43,330
(Glancing)

377
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:44,730
INGYOO and Kasper?

378
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:46,160
The artists they worked with overlap quite a lot.

379
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:47,400
TAEMIN, for one.

380
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:49,970
(Their works with SM Entertainment's artists stand out.)

381
00:13:49,970 --> 00:13:52,000
Kasper should join for sure.

382
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,770
TAEMIN, BAEKHYUN,

383
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:56,410
and SHINee. He's created many masterpieces with them.

384
00:13:56,410 --> 00:13:59,210
NCT, RIIZE, and aespa for me.

385
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:02,810
The current SM boy groups' director...

386
00:14:02,810 --> 00:14:04,950
and SM's director in its early stage, Kasper.

387
00:14:04,950 --> 00:14:06,520
It'll be brutal.

388
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:09,720
Who do you think works most with SM Entertainment?

389
00:14:10,690 --> 00:14:13,960
I think WE DEM BOYZ works with them a lot.

390
00:14:14,330 --> 00:14:15,960
But he's acting too cocky.

391
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:17,860
I'd say I'm pretty good at making...

392
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:19,200
good choreography.

393
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,770
I'll start acting cocky from now.

394
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:24,740
There are many fake directors.

395
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:28,940
We should filter out those.

396
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:31,040
(Kasper)

397
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:33,380
Is there a unique experience you have?

398
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:34,980
- Me? - Yes.

399
00:14:35,510 --> 00:14:37,350
As of now,

400
00:14:37,350 --> 00:14:38,950
it'd be Coachella.

401
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,350
Coachella!

402
00:14:40,350 --> 00:14:44,620
Directing a Coachella performance is all directors' dream.

403
00:14:44,620 --> 00:14:46,360
He was the first K-pop male solo artist...

404
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:48,090
to perform at Coachella.

405
00:14:48,090 --> 00:14:49,460
And I directed the performance.

406
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:51,630
The fact that you have your name credited...

407
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:54,270
as a director for the show which the whole world tunes into...

408
00:14:54,270 --> 00:14:55,630
means you've reached the peak.

409
00:14:55,630 --> 00:14:56,800
For me,

410
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:58,740
I control...

411
00:14:58,740 --> 00:15:01,340
the special effects, lighting, set,

412
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:03,510
in-house volume, set list, title, and so on.

413
00:15:04,170 --> 00:15:06,880
The solo concerts were very well-received too.

414
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:10,650
I'm more confident in performances, concerts, and stages.

415
00:15:10,650 --> 00:15:13,050
I'll show you what a true director is.

416
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,150
Amazing.

417
00:15:15,490 --> 00:15:16,920
Someone arrived.

418
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,820
Someone has arrived.

419
00:15:19,490 --> 00:15:20,820
Renan has arrived.

420
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:24,190
My gosh.

421
00:15:25,130 --> 00:15:26,160
Is it Renan?

422
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:28,870
Renan and I take up...

423
00:15:28,870 --> 00:15:30,100
most of K-pop girl group choreography.

424
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:31,500
I think we're top two.

425
00:15:31,970 --> 00:15:33,570
This is amazing.

426
00:15:33,570 --> 00:15:37,140
Hello. I'm Renan, a choreographer from Japan.

427
00:15:38,010 --> 00:15:40,740
She makes really good girl group choreography.

428
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:43,750
The "Armageddon" choreography was sensational.

429
00:15:43,750 --> 00:15:45,180
(The finger wave of "Armageddon" by aespa)

430
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:46,180
Very unique.

431
00:15:46,180 --> 00:15:48,490
She makes original choreography.

432
00:15:48,590 --> 00:15:51,090
aespa, one of the most popular groups.

433
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:53,390
I first worked with them on the MMA performance,

434
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:55,530
and it was so well-received.

435
00:15:56,190 --> 00:15:59,100
Since then, I've been working with them...

436
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:01,800
on their awards show performances, concerts, and so on.

437
00:16:02,230 --> 00:16:04,270
I know La Chica and Renan...

438
00:16:04,270 --> 00:16:06,340
have worked on the same projects many times.

439
00:16:06,470 --> 00:16:07,970
Mostly with aespa's songs.

440
00:16:08,470 --> 00:16:09,910
"Whiplash" and "LEMONADE."

441
00:16:09,910 --> 00:16:11,940
Who owns "Whiplash?"

442
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:13,110
"Whiplash?"

443
00:16:13,110 --> 00:16:14,750
This is La Chica's move, right?

444
00:16:14,850 --> 00:16:16,850
It's this for "Whiplash."

445
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:18,350
This is the highlight.

446
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:23,120
Many people remember it as La Chica's dance.

447
00:16:23,290 --> 00:16:24,360
But...

448
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:26,390
I choreographed 80 percent of it.

449
00:16:26,590 --> 00:16:29,260
Another neck-grabbing move,

450
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:31,400
KARINA's intro,

451
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:34,330
and the "super GISELLE time" at the end.

452
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:36,670
I made 80 percent of it.

453
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:38,070
I felt very wronged.

454
00:16:38,070 --> 00:16:41,370
Renan choreographed way more of the song than La Chica.

455
00:16:41,370 --> 00:16:44,910
But the highlight was La Chica's.

456
00:16:44,910 --> 00:16:47,880
"Whoever made the highlight owns it." This is what people think.

457
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:49,750
So Renan must feel very disappointed.

458
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:51,520
What can we do? Everyone is dancing this.

459
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:54,080
We took the highlight.

460
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:57,420
They need to decide whose name should be credited first.

461
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:58,460
(Getting his popcorn ready)

462
00:16:58,590 --> 00:17:01,730
Both of them are such formidable opponents,

463
00:17:01,730 --> 00:17:03,390
so I'm scared.

464
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:06,830
(Opening the door)

465
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:10,630
- Hello. - Hello.

466
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:12,870
The rivals have met.

467
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,740
You're now seeing the meeting of two rivals.

468
00:17:17,410 --> 00:17:18,540
You look stunning.

469
00:17:19,110 --> 00:17:20,940
- Seriously. As expected of you. - It's a pink room.

470
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:22,010
You look stunning.

471
00:17:22,010 --> 00:17:23,210
Thank you.

472
00:17:23,610 --> 00:17:25,080
You look stunning.

473
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:27,380
My gosh.

474
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:28,790
They're wary of each other.

475
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:31,690
They're smiling, but you know what's going on.

476
00:17:32,020 --> 00:17:33,890
(A strange tension between them)

477
00:17:33,890 --> 00:17:36,060
- You look stunning. - Since we've met here,

478
00:17:36,060 --> 00:17:37,260
we should have a proper battle.

479
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:40,260
Since we're fighting as directors, I'm very confident.

480
00:17:42,570 --> 00:17:46,100
I'm rather wary of Renan as a director.

481
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,140
Their rooms are next to each other.

482
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:51,110
Who will be next?

483
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:54,240
(The next choreographer strides in, showing off her outstanding height.)

484
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,480
My gosh.

485
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,080
It's been so long since I last saw this.

486
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,190
I'm walking up the stairs for the first time in a while.

487
00:18:07,190 --> 00:18:09,030
BEBE, I miss you guys.

488
00:18:09,730 --> 00:18:13,500
I come from the winning crew, which weighs heavily on me.

489
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:15,800
So I was very resolute.

490
00:18:16,570 --> 00:18:18,100
Congratulations, BEBE!

491
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:19,370
The leader of BEBE,

492
00:18:19,370 --> 00:18:20,670
the winning crew of "Street Woman Fighter 2."

493
00:18:20,670 --> 00:18:22,070
Hello, I'm BADA, a choreographer.

494
00:18:22,510 --> 00:18:25,310
She's the wannabe of many idol singers.

495
00:18:25,310 --> 00:18:28,750
A lot of idol singers want to film a dance challenge with her.

496
00:18:28,810 --> 00:18:30,480
She has long, powerful arms and legs,

497
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:32,280
and she looks so cool when she dances.

498
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:34,050
She really stands out when she dances.

499
00:18:34,050 --> 00:18:35,890
So she's loved by many artists.

500
00:18:35,890 --> 00:18:39,260
I'm probably the most influential choreographer and director.

501
00:18:39,590 --> 00:18:41,960
My ambition as a director grew recently.

502
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:44,030
For "Rover," I took part as the director,

503
00:18:44,030 --> 00:18:45,800
the film director,

504
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:47,870
and the stage production.

505
00:18:48,370 --> 00:18:51,030
I directed the whole of KAI's concert.

506
00:18:51,030 --> 00:18:53,740
I wanted the performances to be immersive.

507
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:57,040
I probably have less experience as a director than the rest,

508
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:58,280
but you better be wary of me.

509
00:18:58,280 --> 00:19:00,340
I'll prove why all the artists chose me...

510
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:01,910
as their director.

511
00:19:02,910 --> 00:19:04,180
This is so cool.

512
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:08,120
It's BADA.

513
00:19:08,990 --> 00:19:10,590
(Everyone welcomes BADA.)

514
00:19:10,590 --> 00:19:12,160
Hi, BADA.

515
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:14,760
(She is just fascinated.)

516
00:19:14,990 --> 00:19:16,860
Hello, BADA.

517
00:19:17,290 --> 00:19:18,930
You're a pink princess today.

518
00:19:18,930 --> 00:19:20,860
Yes, I made everything pink.

519
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:22,030
You're a present.

520
00:19:22,570 --> 00:19:24,030
I'm Orange BABYZOO.

521
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:27,240
Nice to see you.

522
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:29,340
- How have you been? - Good.

523
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:31,070
(Hi, INGYOO.)

524
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:35,350
I really respect BADA as a dancer.

525
00:19:35,850 --> 00:19:38,380
She's a top-tier dancer.

526
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:39,620
Director BADA?

527
00:19:39,620 --> 00:19:41,020
More like a star dancer.

528
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:43,250
I'm not afraid of her as a director.

529
00:19:43,250 --> 00:19:45,290
She's just a star dancer.

530
00:19:45,690 --> 00:19:47,420
BADA, let's do this.

531
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:53,600
To call her a director...

532
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:55,800
She just works with KAI.

533
00:19:55,970 --> 00:19:59,370
Did she do an incredible job of stage directing...

534
00:19:59,940 --> 00:20:03,310
Unless she showed off her skills as a dancer,

535
00:20:03,310 --> 00:20:05,140
the overall stage layout and setup...

536
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:06,780
were messy.

537
00:20:06,910 --> 00:20:09,880
The first thing I see is "winner."

538
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:13,220
I had the honor of winning.

539
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:15,650
What's the point of showing it off?

540
00:20:15,650 --> 00:20:17,790
It's faster to show your skills.

541
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:20,560
Being a good dancer doesn't make you a good director.

542
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:22,760
It's about brains, not body.

543
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:24,960
She won't be a match for me.

544
00:20:25,330 --> 00:20:26,460
This time again,

545
00:20:27,530 --> 00:20:28,830
I'll show you...

546
00:20:28,830 --> 00:20:31,600
how good of a director I can be, not just as BEBE...

547
00:20:32,140 --> 00:20:34,100
and win.

548
00:20:35,170 --> 00:20:37,010
(Who's next?)

549
00:20:37,010 --> 00:20:38,110
Oh, dear.

550
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:39,740
It's all...

551
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:41,310
It's so pretty.

552
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:44,080
I checked if I could turn well.

553
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:48,390
(She even checks the floor. Who is she?)

554
00:20:49,890 --> 00:20:50,890
You feel overwhelmed.

555
00:20:50,890 --> 00:20:52,460
She's the best contemporary choreographer.

556
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:55,730
She really shows what it means to speak with your body.

557
00:20:56,390 --> 00:20:59,500
I'm the founder and director of COME HERE.

558
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,760
I'm Hash, a choreographer.

559
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:04,500
COME HERE specializes in mega crew performance.

560
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:07,640
It's the one-and-only team, which nobody can copy.

561
00:21:07,940 --> 00:21:09,210
(During the choreographer lineup reveal)

562
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:10,240
I got chills.

563
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:11,810
I respect her so much.

564
00:21:11,810 --> 00:21:14,040
She's world class. Her results say it all.

565
00:21:14,210 --> 00:21:15,810
It's the biggest competition.

566
00:21:15,810 --> 00:21:18,280
She won awards both in Korea and overseas.

567
00:21:18,450 --> 00:21:20,850
Not once did I miss an award.

568
00:21:20,850 --> 00:21:22,520
The biggest achievement is...

569
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:24,250
"America's Got Talent."

570
00:21:24,250 --> 00:21:25,720
It's a global show.

571
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:27,260
They're on another level.

572
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:31,800
She's good at making moves that impress people.

573
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:34,600
Perfect synchronization and artistic movements.

574
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:36,230
Mega crew is Hash.

575
00:21:36,230 --> 00:21:37,870
I have no limits.

576
00:21:37,870 --> 00:21:39,300
Skill-wise,

577
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:41,370
I think I'm the best.

578
00:21:41,940 --> 00:21:44,940
A trophy display shelf I made.

579
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:48,780
Hash has a very dense career.

580
00:21:49,450 --> 00:21:51,650
I'm quite curious about JEONG MIN JUN.

581
00:21:51,650 --> 00:21:53,380
I know almost nothing about him.

582
00:21:54,580 --> 00:21:55,590
(Amazed)

583
00:21:56,250 --> 00:21:57,620
This is cool.

584
00:21:58,190 --> 00:21:59,360
Hello.

585
00:21:59,820 --> 00:22:00,920
Hello.

586
00:22:01,890 --> 00:22:02,890
(Skipping)

587
00:22:04,160 --> 00:22:05,430
(The booth at the entrance stands out to him.)

588
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:08,270
(He enters smoothly as if lured by it.)

589
00:22:08,270 --> 00:22:10,630
I'd look around, but I could never actually buy it.

590
00:22:10,930 --> 00:22:12,070
Look at this.

591
00:22:12,070 --> 00:22:14,940
(Suddenly engrossed in shopping)

592
00:22:16,110 --> 00:22:17,210
Pretty, right?

593
00:22:17,410 --> 00:22:18,910
(During the choreographer lineup reveal)

594
00:22:19,910 --> 00:22:21,180
The Stories is here.

595
00:22:21,180 --> 00:22:22,350
(Very shocked)

596
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:24,480
The Stories is joining?

597
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:27,120
Of course I know. They won the overseas competition.

598
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:28,890
Two years in a row.

599
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:29,920
Yes.

600
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:30,990
In terms of stage,

601
00:22:30,990 --> 00:22:33,020
I think they're neck and neck.

602
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:34,660
COME HERE and The Stories.

603
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:37,460
They take part in every competition.

604
00:22:37,660 --> 00:22:39,500
Kalvin Kim, their leader, wound join, right?

605
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:42,430
The soft bear of the amazing team.

606
00:22:42,530 --> 00:22:43,600
Kalvin?

607
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:46,340
(And the hidden champion of the victory)

608
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:48,170
He's really good...

609
00:22:48,170 --> 00:22:49,170
What?

610
00:22:49,570 --> 00:22:50,570
What?

611
00:22:50,570 --> 00:22:52,240
(Who is he?)

612
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:53,610
Who is he?

613
00:22:53,710 --> 00:22:56,180
JEONG MIN JUN?

614
00:22:56,450 --> 00:22:57,980
I don't know him.

615
00:22:57,980 --> 00:22:59,080
Born in 2004.

616
00:22:59,620 --> 00:23:02,190
Why did you pick him? I'm curious.

617
00:23:02,190 --> 00:23:03,790
Things are starting to get boring.

618
00:23:04,220 --> 00:23:05,360
Hello.

619
00:23:05,690 --> 00:23:08,930
I'm on my way to becoming a rising star.

620
00:23:08,930 --> 00:23:10,730
I'm the co-director of The Stories,

621
00:23:10,730 --> 00:23:12,030
JEONG MIN JUN.

622
00:23:12,430 --> 00:23:13,960
I was born in 2004.

623
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:15,900
In 2024, for VIBE,

624
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:18,140
I took part as a section choreographer and won.

625
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:20,940
For the second time we participated, I took part as a co-director.

626
00:23:20,940 --> 00:23:22,410
We won twice.

627
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:24,010
The first Koreans to win.

628
00:23:24,010 --> 00:23:25,080
It's the best career.

629
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:27,680
Only MIN JUN can change the game.

630
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:29,380
I have the skills...

631
00:23:29,380 --> 00:23:32,250
in staging, directing, and overseeing the dancers.

632
00:23:32,250 --> 00:23:34,950
They clearly trusted my skills.

633
00:23:34,950 --> 00:23:36,920
I'm the next-generation director.

634
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:41,260
(Pause)

635
00:23:41,690 --> 00:23:43,030
Hello.

636
00:23:43,460 --> 00:23:45,900
(All eyes on him)

637
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:49,200
(He hides himself next to the wall as he walks in awkwardly.)

638
00:23:50,070 --> 00:23:52,670
He's so young. What can he show us?

639
00:23:53,740 --> 00:23:55,470
(His mouth gets dry.)

640
00:23:55,470 --> 00:23:57,410
I'm too nervous. What do I do?

641
00:23:57,870 --> 00:23:58,980
Hello.

642
00:23:59,180 --> 00:24:00,380
(Staring)

643
00:24:00,380 --> 00:24:03,650
Main director and co-director are very different, actually.

644
00:24:04,210 --> 00:24:06,120
He must be the weakest among us.

645
00:24:06,350 --> 00:24:08,420
All he has is his youth.

646
00:24:09,150 --> 00:24:10,150
Hello.
(The youngest isn't done with his greeting tour.)

647
00:24:11,150 --> 00:24:14,790
A crew member came to represent his crew, not the leader.

648
00:24:14,830 --> 00:24:16,430
I think he's weak.

649
00:24:16,430 --> 00:24:18,430
I'll have to see what he does.

650
00:24:19,630 --> 00:24:21,230
- Hello. - Hi.

651
00:24:22,570 --> 00:24:24,970
He's a choreographer, basically. Not a director.

652
00:24:25,700 --> 00:24:28,410
He must be grateful to have this opportunity.

653
00:24:28,410 --> 00:24:29,870
He'll learn a lot from here.

654
00:24:33,910 --> 00:24:35,510
What I felt was...

655
00:24:35,510 --> 00:24:36,710
that it's so competitive.

656
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:40,080
You can't smile and act friendly.

657
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:41,850
(Gulping)

658
00:24:41,990 --> 00:24:44,390
Actually, I'm not that intimidated.

659
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:46,520
If you put K-pop choreography...

660
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:48,560
against choreography meant for competitions,

661
00:24:49,160 --> 00:24:51,660
the competition choreography will win without a doubt.

662
00:24:51,730 --> 00:24:52,930
I should win.

663
00:24:54,130 --> 00:24:56,200
Who hasn't arrived yet?

664
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:57,730
Just Koo Young.

665
00:24:59,170 --> 00:25:02,710
For directing, you can't ignore the database you've built.

666
00:25:02,710 --> 00:25:04,610
He probably has the most data.

667
00:25:04,840 --> 00:25:06,480
Why are you joining?

668
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:09,080
He is joining, after all.

669
00:25:09,080 --> 00:25:10,710
Back Koo Young is a legend.

670
00:25:10,710 --> 00:25:13,650
You can't leave him out in a battle of directors.

671
00:25:13,950 --> 00:25:14,950
Hello.

672
00:25:14,950 --> 00:25:17,490
I'm Back Koo Young, a choreographer for 24 years.

673
00:25:18,020 --> 00:25:19,220
"Twenty-four years?"

674
00:25:19,220 --> 00:25:21,120
That's more years than my age.

675
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:23,790
Experience-wise, nobody can beat him.

676
00:25:24,060 --> 00:25:26,730
He was the core of SM Entertainment's performance.

677
00:25:26,930 --> 00:25:29,800
Every SM Entertainment artist from that time...

678
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:31,840
was directed by Koo Young.

679
00:25:32,070 --> 00:25:35,570
When I was in SM, I directed all the awards show stages too.

680
00:25:35,870 --> 00:25:37,870
He's up here.

681
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:39,640
The textbook example of boy groups.

682
00:25:40,840 --> 00:25:42,450
On "Road to Kingdom,"

683
00:25:42,450 --> 00:25:45,380
I saw how he made THE BOYZ popular with his directing.

684
00:25:45,380 --> 00:25:46,580
His work is extremely high quality.

685
00:25:46,950 --> 00:25:48,690
(Koo Young led THE BOYZ to their victory and heyday.)

686
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:50,690
I became THE BOYZ's director...

687
00:25:50,690 --> 00:25:52,590
and directed ZENERATION Two.

688
00:25:52,590 --> 00:25:54,190
He makes incredible use of the stage.

689
00:25:54,190 --> 00:25:55,990
He's very experienced.

690
00:25:55,990 --> 00:25:58,330
He caused a big impact performance-wise...

691
00:25:58,330 --> 00:26:01,500
and led the changes. Nobody can deny that.

692
00:26:01,630 --> 00:26:03,800
I'm good, obviously. I've been doing this for so long.

693
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:06,300
It's different from unwarranted confidence.

694
00:26:09,310 --> 00:26:12,280
(The last person to enter Directors' Lab is Back Koo Young.)

695
00:26:12,780 --> 00:26:13,910
(Koo Young came back.)

696
00:26:14,140 --> 00:26:15,610
Hello.

697
00:26:16,550 --> 00:26:17,980
Hello, Koo Young.

698
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:19,580
The veteran has arrived.

699
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:21,120
Hello.

700
00:26:21,950 --> 00:26:23,120
Hello.

701
00:26:23,850 --> 00:26:24,960
Hello, Koo Young.

702
00:26:25,160 --> 00:26:26,220
Brother.

703
00:26:26,220 --> 00:26:27,490
It's been a while.

704
00:26:28,930 --> 00:26:30,530
- Are you going to win? - I must win.

705
00:26:30,530 --> 00:26:31,860
Aren't you all here to win?

706
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:34,260
This is the beginning.

707
00:26:34,830 --> 00:26:37,230
This is the ultimate war of the champions.

708
00:26:37,230 --> 00:26:39,200
Regardless of gender,

709
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:43,310
in here, it's a battle fought purely on a director's skills.

710
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:45,410
And seeing all these top-tier...

711
00:26:45,410 --> 00:26:48,110
choreographers and directors gathered in one place,

712
00:26:48,280 --> 00:26:49,480
I was overwhelmed.

713
00:26:50,280 --> 00:26:52,380
Someone will keep proving themselves here, right?

714
00:26:52,650 --> 00:26:53,920
And I need to show what I've got too.

715
00:26:54,420 --> 00:26:56,650
I'll destroy them all if anyone messes with me.

716
00:26:57,120 --> 00:26:59,690
I have to compete against other choreographers.

717
00:27:01,290 --> 00:27:03,490
When it's time, I've got to do it right like they do.

718
00:27:05,460 --> 00:27:08,670
These spaces are quite exposed, with all this glass.

719
00:27:08,930 --> 00:27:09,970
It's really...

720
00:27:10,800 --> 00:27:11,970
That scared me.

721
00:27:12,470 --> 00:27:13,470
What?

722
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:15,470
What was that?

723
00:27:15,670 --> 00:27:17,340
(A siren echoes throughout the entire square.)

724
00:27:17,340 --> 00:27:18,940
- What is it? - Emergency.

725
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,410
(What is it?)

726
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:23,050
Emergency.

727
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:25,180
What is going on?

728
00:27:25,180 --> 00:27:26,350
Oh, dear.

729
00:27:28,150 --> 00:27:29,690
(Please come out to the square now.)

730
00:27:29,990 --> 00:27:31,790
"Please come out to the square now."

731
00:27:31,790 --> 00:27:33,090
Come out to the square?

732
00:27:33,720 --> 00:27:34,960
I'll head out then.

733
00:27:34,960 --> 00:27:36,290
Okay. Let's go.

734
00:27:38,660 --> 00:27:40,060
Emergency.

735
00:27:40,060 --> 00:27:41,730
(The 10 choreographers gather in the square.)

736
00:27:41,900 --> 00:27:43,730
What's going on? I felt a bit anxious.

737
00:27:44,370 --> 00:27:45,700
My goodness.

738
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:48,970
Seeing each other out in the open,

739
00:27:48,970 --> 00:27:50,240
I was really terrified.

740
00:27:51,070 --> 00:27:52,510
This is insane.

741
00:27:52,510 --> 00:27:55,950
All the top-tier choreographers...

742
00:27:55,950 --> 00:27:57,880
and directors are brought together.

743
00:27:58,680 --> 00:28:01,080
So I got a bit intimidated.

744
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:05,790
I guessed what mission it would be, but at the same time, I had no clue.

745
00:28:05,790 --> 00:28:08,730
I thought that I shouldn't let my guard down for a single moment.

746
00:28:10,630 --> 00:28:12,200
(What?)

747
00:28:14,660 --> 00:28:15,700
This is amazing!

748
00:28:16,470 --> 00:28:17,570
- You look so cool. - You look so cool.

749
00:28:17,570 --> 00:28:18,670
You look great.

750
00:28:19,300 --> 00:28:21,770
A directing war where choreographers battle through masterworks,

751
00:28:21,770 --> 00:28:23,610
going beyond performances.

752
00:28:23,970 --> 00:28:27,180
Hello, I am Sung Hanbin, the MC for the Mnet original dance series,

753
00:28:27,180 --> 00:28:30,750
Street World Fighter: Directors' War.

754
00:28:33,950 --> 00:28:35,450
A stage where the outcome is decided...

755
00:28:35,450 --> 00:28:39,060
not under a crew's name, but by a single individual.

756
00:28:39,190 --> 00:28:41,160
In every mission,

757
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:44,290
the choreographers will compete for one exclusive spot.

758
00:28:44,430 --> 00:28:45,430
My goodness.

759
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:48,800
That is the Director Credit,

760
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:50,570
naming the ultimate master of the performance.

761
00:28:53,070 --> 00:28:54,240
Credit Board?

762
00:28:54,470 --> 00:28:55,910
The Credit Board is...

763
00:28:55,910 --> 00:28:59,680
where the name of the sole director who claims the final performance...

764
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:02,110
along with the choreographers...

765
00:29:02,110 --> 00:29:05,380
who brought it to life together will be recorded.

766
00:29:05,380 --> 00:29:07,750
So the credits are written differently.

767
00:29:08,050 --> 00:29:09,390
They're under different names.

768
00:29:09,390 --> 00:29:11,420
Putting a choreographer's name below the director...

769
00:29:11,420 --> 00:29:13,420
really hurts your pride.

770
00:29:13,420 --> 00:29:14,490
That's so cruel.

771
00:29:14,490 --> 00:29:15,630
It means you might just create the choreography...

772
00:29:15,630 --> 00:29:17,160
and get completely cut off from directing.

773
00:29:17,160 --> 00:29:18,230
Exactly.

774
00:29:18,290 --> 00:29:19,730
The dance scene is...

775
00:29:19,730 --> 00:29:22,170
really sensitive about credits.

776
00:29:22,330 --> 00:29:25,200
The order of names changes depending on the level of contribution.

777
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:28,240
The director's name is put front in big, bold letters,

778
00:29:28,240 --> 00:29:30,870
and below that, the choreographers are written in smaller print.

779
00:29:30,870 --> 00:29:34,780
Wouldn't you want your name written in the bigger spot?

780
00:29:34,840 --> 00:29:37,380
I came here for a directors' battle, so I have to become the director.

781
00:29:37,380 --> 00:29:40,150
We're already doing the choreography work anyway.

782
00:29:40,220 --> 00:29:41,580
I'm confident about getting on the Director Credit.

783
00:29:41,580 --> 00:29:44,450
I've always had my name go up there.

784
00:29:44,720 --> 00:29:46,760
I thought, "That's mine." And at the same time,

785
00:29:46,760 --> 00:29:48,590
I knew I had to take it no matter what.

786
00:29:48,590 --> 00:29:50,660
I must become the director, no matter what.

787
00:29:50,660 --> 00:29:53,600
I was a born director.

788
00:29:54,130 --> 00:29:57,830
In this place, both skill and outcome are...

789
00:29:58,200 --> 00:30:02,270
proven by whether your name remains or disappears.

790
00:30:02,270 --> 00:30:04,110
- Why are you doing this? - Gosh, seriously...

791
00:30:04,110 --> 00:30:05,440
This is too harsh.

792
00:30:05,440 --> 00:30:07,040
Now they're just deleting our names.

793
00:30:07,110 --> 00:30:08,210
(Flustered)

794
00:30:08,240 --> 00:30:09,680
This is interesting.

795
00:30:09,750 --> 00:30:12,020
They really know how to get on our nerves.

796
00:30:12,020 --> 00:30:14,120
Everyone here came to be a director.

797
00:30:15,420 --> 00:30:17,390
So they're provoking us like this?

798
00:30:17,390 --> 00:30:19,920
They try to hurt our pride like this?

799
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:22,390
They know exactly what triggers us.

800
00:30:22,390 --> 00:30:23,690
Darn it.

801
00:30:24,360 --> 00:30:28,060
And the first directing mission to kick it all off.

802
00:30:28,230 --> 00:30:32,570
The 1-on-1 Signature Mission.

803
00:30:32,670 --> 00:30:34,070
What does that mean?

804
00:30:34,070 --> 00:30:36,870
Are we battling with our own signature performances?

805
00:30:36,870 --> 00:30:38,110
It's a 1-on-1 battle.

806
00:30:38,310 --> 00:30:40,380
The 1-on-1 Signature Mission...

807
00:30:40,380 --> 00:30:42,610
consists of a two-stage battle.

808
00:30:42,610 --> 00:30:45,620
The first stage is the Signature Choreography Takeover Match.

809
00:30:45,620 --> 00:30:46,620
A takeover match?

810
00:30:46,620 --> 00:30:47,880
So we steal it.

811
00:30:47,920 --> 00:30:49,550
The signature choreography match...

812
00:30:49,550 --> 00:30:52,190
is a face-off where you recreate your opponent's signature moves...

813
00:30:52,190 --> 00:30:55,120
to steal their original signature choreography.

814
00:30:55,290 --> 00:30:58,490
The winning choreographer keeps their own signature choreography...

815
00:30:58,490 --> 00:31:00,900
and seizes their opponent's.

816
00:31:00,930 --> 00:31:04,200
The losing choreographer loses their own signature choreography...

817
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:06,970
and must prepare for the next round using the version...

818
00:31:06,970 --> 00:31:08,470
recreated by their opponent.

819
00:31:09,140 --> 00:31:10,710
- I knew it. - My goodness.

820
00:31:11,110 --> 00:31:12,980
That's really cruel.

821
00:31:12,980 --> 00:31:14,010
I lose my signature moves?

822
00:31:14,010 --> 00:31:15,850
- Yes, you lose it. - That's it.

823
00:31:16,310 --> 00:31:18,080
I lose it? It's deleted?

824
00:31:18,280 --> 00:31:21,620
My "Love Shot" choreography gets wiped out?

825
00:31:22,320 --> 00:31:24,150
I can't even imagine that.

826
00:31:24,420 --> 00:31:27,120
Who would ever want my hard work to go down the drain?

827
00:31:27,860 --> 00:31:30,130
I definitely have to win this.

828
00:31:30,560 --> 00:31:33,830
However, winning the signature choreography match...

829
00:31:33,830 --> 00:31:36,230
does not mean you become the final director.

830
00:31:36,970 --> 00:31:38,400
(What?)

831
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:40,200
My goodness.

832
00:31:40,670 --> 00:31:42,070
What else is there?

833
00:31:42,070 --> 00:31:43,140
The two choreographers will determine...

834
00:31:43,140 --> 00:31:47,080
the ultimate winner of each matchup through the Last Run.

835
00:31:47,210 --> 00:31:48,510
Last Run?

836
00:31:48,650 --> 00:31:50,610
Why are there so many hurdles to clear to become the director?

837
00:31:51,210 --> 00:31:53,780
The Last Run is a showdown where choreographers compete...

838
00:31:53,780 --> 00:31:55,650
with a fully realized masterwork,

839
00:31:55,650 --> 00:31:58,590
utilizing dancers to direct moves and formation...

840
00:31:58,590 --> 00:32:01,160
based on the choreography decided in the takeover match.

841
00:32:01,390 --> 00:32:03,430
The choreographer who wins the Last Run...

842
00:32:03,430 --> 00:32:06,360
will have their name listed as a director in the credits...

843
00:32:06,360 --> 00:32:08,600
and perform the performance before an audience.

844
00:32:08,600 --> 00:32:12,300
And the losing choreographer fails to claim the director credit,

845
00:32:12,300 --> 00:32:14,970
and their performance will vanish right away.

846
00:32:15,810 --> 00:32:17,540
- My goodness. - It's so brutal.

847
00:32:17,540 --> 00:32:18,880
It will vanish?

848
00:32:19,140 --> 00:32:21,540
Then what happens to the dancers who practice with us?

849
00:32:21,540 --> 00:32:23,480
If that happens, I don't think I could ever show my face again.

850
00:32:24,980 --> 00:32:29,050
I'm fine, but I feel bad that you guys are heartbroken.

851
00:32:29,050 --> 00:32:31,350
Everyone puts a lot of effort into this performance,

852
00:32:31,350 --> 00:32:33,190
so working so hard for it...

853
00:32:33,190 --> 00:32:36,860
only to say, as a director, "We can't go on stage..."

854
00:32:37,190 --> 00:32:38,290
My goodness.

855
00:32:40,500 --> 00:32:43,430
I think it would bring such crushing disappointment...

856
00:32:43,430 --> 00:32:45,970
to the dancers who trusted and followed only me.

857
00:32:47,170 --> 00:32:50,040
If it actually happens, I'll have a mental breakdown.

858
00:32:50,040 --> 00:32:52,840
If I can't bring the performance to the stage...

859
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:56,010
I never want to let the situation happen.

860
00:32:57,810 --> 00:33:00,180
The most crucial directing element in the 1-on-1 Signature Mission...

861
00:33:00,180 --> 00:33:02,890
is none other than...

862
00:33:02,890 --> 00:33:04,120
the number of dancers.

863
00:33:04,150 --> 00:33:05,960
- What does that mean? - The number of dancers?

864
00:33:06,090 --> 00:33:07,690
Do we need to gather a lot of dancers?

865
00:33:07,690 --> 00:33:09,260
So it's a mega crew performance from the start?

866
00:33:09,260 --> 00:33:10,290
I know.

867
00:33:10,290 --> 00:33:11,530
A mega crew performance from the beginning.

868
00:33:11,530 --> 00:33:13,930
We will now reveal the number of dancers...

869
00:33:13,930 --> 00:33:15,670
for this mission.

870
00:33:15,670 --> 00:33:17,500
- Please. - Please.

871
00:33:17,500 --> 00:33:19,300
Please let it be under 100 people.

872
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:26,740
Stop it!

873
00:33:26,740 --> 00:33:28,380
- Stop! - Stop!

874
00:33:28,380 --> 00:33:29,980
Stop it!

875
00:33:29,980 --> 00:33:31,450
- Stop! - What?

876
00:33:31,450 --> 00:33:32,720
(They can't believe their eyes.)

877
00:33:33,320 --> 00:33:34,320
What?

878
00:33:34,450 --> 00:33:38,050
(Just how high is that number going?)

879
00:33:38,220 --> 00:33:39,220
What?

880
00:33:41,160 --> 00:33:42,630
(No way.)

881
00:33:42,790 --> 00:33:43,830
What?

882
00:33:44,630 --> 00:33:45,630
It's 400 people?

883
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:48,600
Does it make sense that we need 400 dancers?

884
00:33:49,170 --> 00:33:51,670
I couldn't believe it, so I kept looking at the number.

885
00:33:51,670 --> 00:33:55,640
Doing a mega crew performance right from the start fazed me.

886
00:33:55,940 --> 00:33:57,170
This must be a lie.

887
00:33:57,170 --> 00:33:59,640
There's no way they gathered 400 people.

888
00:33:59,640 --> 00:34:01,980
So, 400 dancers are coming here?

889
00:34:04,110 --> 00:34:05,580
My gosh. That scared me.

890
00:34:06,080 --> 00:34:09,250
The production scale just got massive.

891
00:34:09,590 --> 00:34:10,790
It's kind of terrifying.

892
00:34:11,190 --> 00:34:12,260
It's AI, right?

893
00:34:13,090 --> 00:34:14,320
Are they standing outside?

894
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:15,660
This is the hallway.

895
00:34:15,660 --> 00:34:19,560
Please head out to the lobby now...

896
00:34:19,900 --> 00:34:22,370
- to check the dancers' profiles. - This is crazy.

897
00:34:22,370 --> 00:34:23,930
- What? - Let's go.

898
00:34:23,930 --> 00:34:25,940
- Hey, let's go. - Are they standing out there?

899
00:34:26,370 --> 00:34:27,540
Let's just go and see.

900
00:34:27,540 --> 00:34:29,040
- They're here now? - Let's go.

901
00:34:29,040 --> 00:34:31,410
- Let's just go. - It's insane.

902
00:34:31,410 --> 00:34:32,510
(With no time to process the shock, the choreographers rush out.)

903
00:34:32,940 --> 00:34:34,510
We need to check the dancers' profiles.

904
00:34:34,780 --> 00:34:36,480
(Moving outside to check the dancers' profiles)

905
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:38,210
- Unbelievable. - There are a lot.

906
00:34:41,420 --> 00:34:42,750
It's 400 people.

907
00:34:44,150 --> 00:34:46,190
I thought it was an AI-generated image.

908
00:34:46,420 --> 00:34:47,590
The scale is insane.

909
00:34:47,590 --> 00:34:48,620
Unbelievable.

910
00:34:48,620 --> 00:34:49,960
It's endless.

911
00:34:50,230 --> 00:34:52,090
no:ze? Vata?

912
00:34:52,230 --> 00:34:53,430
- no:ze? - no:ze?

913
00:34:53,430 --> 00:34:55,130
- It's Vata. - Seriously?

914
00:34:55,130 --> 00:34:57,070
- Is Shuri coming? - Shuri is coming as well?

915
00:34:57,230 --> 00:34:59,300
For a director, which players...

916
00:34:59,300 --> 00:35:02,210
and which dancers you work with is crucial.

917
00:35:02,210 --> 00:35:04,810
Since this mission is a mega crew performance,

918
00:35:04,810 --> 00:35:07,880
those with extensive experience in award shows or mega crew work...

919
00:35:07,880 --> 00:35:10,180
will probably have an advantage.

920
00:35:10,180 --> 00:35:13,550
I definitely want dancers whose main genre is choreography.

921
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:18,090
There's a huge difference between those with...

922
00:35:18,090 --> 00:35:20,660
competition experience and those without.

923
00:35:20,660 --> 00:35:22,360
Rather than a preferred genre,

924
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:24,960
I like dancers who have distinct character.

925
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:27,300
What matters is that the dancer has star quality.

926
00:35:27,300 --> 00:35:30,700
I want someone who masters many genres or has a broad spectrum.

927
00:35:30,870 --> 00:35:33,170
- Is Jinwoo coming? - My goodness.

928
00:35:33,170 --> 00:35:34,670
I'll bring Jinwoo.

929
00:35:34,840 --> 00:35:36,110
I'll take him with me.

930
00:35:36,110 --> 00:35:38,270
- No, he's mine. - I'll bring him.

931
00:35:38,270 --> 00:35:42,380
I consider the mega crew mission itself to be the highlight.

932
00:35:42,480 --> 00:35:45,980
There's a beauty only large-scale performances can deliver.

933
00:35:45,980 --> 00:35:48,580
And we're doing that from Episode One? Awesome.

934
00:35:48,580 --> 00:35:49,720
With 400 dancers?

935
00:35:49,890 --> 00:35:51,350
I'm confident.

936
00:35:51,350 --> 00:35:53,260
I'm a little nervous.

937
00:35:53,260 --> 00:35:55,260
Just how far can I really go?

938
00:35:55,260 --> 00:35:58,960
I want to hear people say, "Whatever Koo Young creates is..."

939
00:35:58,960 --> 00:36:00,630
"a true work of art and a masterpiece."

940
00:36:01,930 --> 00:36:05,170
This mission is a battle to prove performances...

941
00:36:05,170 --> 00:36:07,670
that transcend signature styles through directing.

942
00:36:07,840 --> 00:36:10,910
And depending on the outcome, you may remain...

943
00:36:10,910 --> 00:36:12,880
merely a choreographer,

944
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:16,050
or you may earn your name on the Director Credit.

945
00:36:16,280 --> 00:36:18,780
But what's crucial is that...

946
00:36:18,780 --> 00:36:22,720
your fate can completely change depending on whom you face.

947
00:36:24,190 --> 00:36:26,360
The 1-on-1 Signature Mission.

948
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:30,260
You've already evaluated each other's skills in pre-shoots,

949
00:36:30,360 --> 00:36:32,660
and all the matchups are set.

950
00:36:33,200 --> 00:36:34,330
I guess they're revealing them now.

951
00:36:34,330 --> 00:36:35,800
Oh, no!

952
00:36:36,270 --> 00:36:37,500
We will now reveal...

953
00:36:37,500 --> 00:36:40,470
the choreographers for the first matchup.

954
00:36:40,470 --> 00:36:41,740
My goodness!

955
00:36:41,740 --> 00:36:43,470
- Oh, no! - What do we do?

956
00:36:43,470 --> 00:36:44,470
Let's go!

957
00:36:44,470 --> 00:36:46,140
- I'm so nervous. - Who would it be?

958
00:36:49,410 --> 00:36:50,410
(Smiling)

959
00:36:50,410 --> 00:36:51,450
Simeez.

960
00:36:51,650 --> 00:36:53,020
Who do you think you'll go up against?

961
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:54,750
No matter who I face, I'm confident.

962
00:36:55,820 --> 00:36:57,920
Simeez has that distinct look in her eyes.

963
00:36:58,050 --> 00:36:59,120
That gaze.

964
00:36:59,120 --> 00:37:01,360
- Seriously. - It's really scary.

965
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:03,360
She is on another level.

966
00:37:03,360 --> 00:37:04,590
She's a professional.

967
00:37:05,060 --> 00:37:06,500
She has plenty of experience too.

968
00:37:06,800 --> 00:37:08,200
That feels pretty good to hear.

969
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:09,570
But...

970
00:37:10,430 --> 00:37:12,500
when I watched "Street Woman Fighter,"

971
00:37:12,500 --> 00:37:16,710
I didn't really feel that La Chica was a skilled crew.

972
00:37:16,940 --> 00:37:18,270
(She mentioned...)

973
00:37:18,270 --> 00:37:19,280
(La Chica?)

974
00:37:20,180 --> 00:37:23,280
I came in thinking, "No one would dare belittle La Chica."

975
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:26,550
So people actually criticize the greatest achievement...

976
00:37:26,550 --> 00:37:28,050
and biggest pride of my life.

977
00:37:28,450 --> 00:37:29,750
I know La Chica's choreography,

978
00:37:29,750 --> 00:37:31,650
but what is Simeez's choreography?

979
00:37:31,790 --> 00:37:33,520
What kind of nonsense is that now?

980
00:37:33,920 --> 00:37:37,130
I've seen La Chica in the credits, but I've never seen Simeez.

981
00:37:37,230 --> 00:37:41,130
How many solo pieces has she even done on her own?

982
00:37:42,370 --> 00:37:43,500
That sounds scary.

983
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:45,530
Probably way more than you.

984
00:37:45,840 --> 00:37:49,510
She's shown her capability as a team rather than as an individual.

985
00:37:49,540 --> 00:37:50,840
If I had three heads working together,

986
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:52,540
I feel like I could make as many as I wanted.

987
00:37:52,980 --> 00:37:54,040
(Eyes shaking)

988
00:37:54,080 --> 00:37:55,650
Is it okay to say things like that?

989
00:37:55,850 --> 00:37:57,680
It's just ridiculous.

990
00:37:57,680 --> 00:37:59,450
Honestly, you've got to admit what's true.

991
00:37:59,620 --> 00:38:01,550
This is a battle you fight alone.

992
00:38:02,720 --> 00:38:03,950
I don't think...

993
00:38:03,950 --> 00:38:05,490
Simeez will even be my competitor.

994
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:07,490
I don't think Simeez will even be my competitor.

995
00:38:08,390 --> 00:38:09,760
This is absurd.

996
00:38:09,960 --> 00:38:10,960
(I can't watch this.)

997
00:38:11,260 --> 00:38:12,800
This is brutal.

998
00:38:13,330 --> 00:38:16,130
I'm curious to see just how much she can pull off on her own here.

999
00:38:17,130 --> 00:38:18,730
She looks dead serious right now.

1000
00:38:18,830 --> 00:38:21,040
She looked completely furious.

1001
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:22,370
What do we do?

1002
00:38:22,970 --> 00:38:25,780
I've never seen anyone ask me a question like that.

1003
00:38:26,040 --> 00:38:28,310
It feels like they don't know a single thing about me.

1004
00:38:28,310 --> 00:38:30,810
I'm going to show them what I've got this time.

1005
00:38:31,110 --> 00:38:32,620
The matchup I want to see is...

1006
00:38:32,620 --> 00:38:34,050
Simeez and Renan.

1007
00:38:34,050 --> 00:38:36,390
The two have had quite a lot of overlapping work.

1008
00:38:36,390 --> 00:38:37,390
Renan and Simeez.

1009
00:38:37,390 --> 00:38:39,220
Simeez and Renan.

1010
00:38:39,220 --> 00:38:40,760
Should we call it a rival match?

1011
00:38:40,760 --> 00:38:42,060
I think it will be a big match.

1012
00:38:42,120 --> 00:38:45,530
Since the two choreographed "Whiplash" together...

1013
00:38:45,530 --> 00:38:47,660
They already have a history of competing with each other.

1014
00:38:47,660 --> 00:38:49,730
The Grand Prize Choreographer of the Year goes...

1015
00:38:49,730 --> 00:38:51,130
to La Chica's "Whiplash."

1016
00:38:51,130 --> 00:38:52,570
With "Whiplash," La Chica won...

1017
00:38:52,570 --> 00:38:54,500
the Grand Prize Choreographer of the Year.

1018
00:38:54,500 --> 00:38:55,910
- What about it? - But...

1019
00:38:55,910 --> 00:38:58,770
about 80 percent of "Whiplash" was my choreography.

1020
00:38:58,970 --> 00:39:00,980
Wouldn't it have been right for me to win the award?

1021
00:39:01,380 --> 00:39:03,450
I just can't understand it even now.

1022
00:39:03,680 --> 00:39:06,150
Then you should've done a better job creating the point choreography.

1023
00:39:06,150 --> 00:39:08,050
Even if she did 80 percent of the work,

1024
00:39:08,050 --> 00:39:10,420
the point choreography was La Chica's.

1025
00:39:11,190 --> 00:39:13,320
This is La Chica's choreography.

1026
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:15,320
When you think of "Whiplash," this is the move.

1027
00:39:15,390 --> 00:39:17,590
"Whiplash." The Neck Hernia Dance.

1028
00:39:18,030 --> 00:39:19,500
You have to admit what's true.

1029
00:39:19,500 --> 00:39:21,960
What can you do? We took the killing part.

1030
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:23,270
I felt deeply wronged.

1031
00:39:23,370 --> 00:39:26,070
I taught all the lessons, and I went to the music video shoot.

1032
00:39:26,070 --> 00:39:27,170
That's true.

1033
00:39:27,240 --> 00:39:29,040
- I went to the broadcast promotion. - She's right.

1034
00:39:29,040 --> 00:39:31,310
And I directed everything when filming the practice video.

1035
00:39:31,310 --> 00:39:33,040
I went to all the TV shows too.

1036
00:39:33,140 --> 00:39:34,180
That's true.

1037
00:39:35,180 --> 00:39:37,250
She must have felt pretty wronged.

1038
00:39:37,250 --> 00:39:39,120
It definitely was a situation where Renan would feel wronged.

1039
00:39:39,350 --> 00:39:41,580
When you get pushed aside just because of the chorus part...

1040
00:39:41,580 --> 00:39:43,220
When the spotlight is stolen away because of the point choreography.

1041
00:39:43,220 --> 00:39:44,620
That's when I get the most furious.

1042
00:39:44,750 --> 00:39:46,690
I cried after that award ceremony was over.

1043
00:39:46,920 --> 00:39:48,160
She cried because of us?

1044
00:39:48,290 --> 00:39:50,490
That feeling of being wronged lingered for a long time.

1045
00:39:50,490 --> 00:39:52,230
Renan did all the hard work,

1046
00:39:52,230 --> 00:39:55,330
but La Chica took all the fame.

1047
00:39:56,300 --> 00:39:58,070
I acknowledge Renan's contribution.

1048
00:39:58,070 --> 00:40:00,300
And it's true that we took the fame.

1049
00:40:00,940 --> 00:40:02,070
But honestly,

1050
00:40:02,070 --> 00:40:04,410
what comes to your mind when you think of "Whiplash?"

1051
00:40:05,610 --> 00:40:07,180
(They perform the Neck Hernia Dance right away.)

1052
00:40:07,510 --> 00:40:08,740
(What can you do about it?)

1053
00:40:09,350 --> 00:40:11,580
I'm just so mad.

1054
00:40:12,310 --> 00:40:15,920
It was the first time I'd ever seen that venomous look on Renan's face.

1055
00:40:16,190 --> 00:40:17,750
It kept burning up inside me.

1056
00:40:17,750 --> 00:40:19,760
The anger is still lingering.

1057
00:40:19,990 --> 00:40:22,220
We need to go head-to-head. I'm confident.

1058
00:40:23,190 --> 00:40:24,190
She's confident?

1059
00:40:24,190 --> 00:40:25,230
I am confident too.

1060
00:40:26,760 --> 00:40:28,160
Let's get it!

1061
00:40:28,160 --> 00:40:29,300
(A big match)

1062
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:31,470
- It will be fun. - It's a big match.

1063
00:40:31,570 --> 00:40:34,300
This is a matchup where no one can predict who will win.

1064
00:40:34,400 --> 00:40:36,910
In the 1-on-1 Signature Mission,

1065
00:40:36,910 --> 00:40:38,240
I bet Renan will win.

1066
00:40:38,740 --> 00:40:39,840
It was just funny.

1067
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:41,340
I'm definitely going to win.

1068
00:40:41,340 --> 00:40:44,050
Where she truly shines is the killing part.

1069
00:40:44,050 --> 00:40:46,680
She knows how to nail the key points.

1070
00:40:46,680 --> 00:40:50,150
She's good at creating choreography that grabs your focus.

1071
00:40:50,150 --> 00:40:52,320
I'm confident when it comes to point choreography.

1072
00:40:52,320 --> 00:40:53,320
But...
(But?)

1073
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:57,360
Aside from that, when I think of Renan's choreography,

1074
00:40:57,360 --> 00:40:59,600
nothing comes to mind other than the point moves.

1075
00:40:59,760 --> 00:41:00,760
(That's harsh.)

1076
00:41:01,930 --> 00:41:03,230
(What did you say?)

1077
00:41:03,230 --> 00:41:04,730
Can you even make point moves?

1078
00:41:04,770 --> 00:41:05,940
(Shocked)

1079
00:41:05,970 --> 00:41:08,440
Renan only has point moves and nothing else.

1080
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:10,940
Renan feels like a bedroom choreographer.

1081
00:41:11,210 --> 00:41:12,840
Isn't she just a closet dancer?

1082
00:41:13,040 --> 00:41:15,810
A closet dancer? That's just too harsh.

1083
00:41:15,810 --> 00:41:16,810
(Walking on eggshells)

1084
00:41:16,810 --> 00:41:18,610
She just moves within 3.3m².

1085
00:41:18,610 --> 00:41:19,620
She goes like this.

1086
00:41:19,620 --> 00:41:21,080
(She moves only her upper body like this.)

1087
00:41:21,080 --> 00:41:22,650
A dance performed purely in a 3.3m² space.

1088
00:41:22,650 --> 00:41:24,390
That was really offensive.

1089
00:41:24,390 --> 00:41:25,860
Doing all the moves in one spot like this.

1090
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:27,690
Or doing all the moves in shoulders?

1091
00:41:27,890 --> 00:41:30,330
It would be well-suited for short-form content, then.

1092
00:41:31,090 --> 00:41:32,600
(Frozen)

1093
00:41:33,060 --> 00:41:34,560
(Shocked)

1094
00:41:35,730 --> 00:41:37,300
I couldn't maintain a poker face at all.

1095
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:38,970
But that's true.

1096
00:41:39,170 --> 00:41:40,570
(Giving up on watching)

1097
00:41:40,900 --> 00:41:42,200
(Brutal)

1098
00:41:42,300 --> 00:41:43,770
I thought the two of them would get into a fight.

1099
00:41:43,940 --> 00:41:46,480
They might actually end up fighting.

1100
00:41:47,740 --> 00:41:50,110
(Amidst the chilling tension,)

1101
00:41:50,110 --> 00:41:51,480
(Renan suddenly grabs the mic.)

1102
00:41:52,720 --> 00:41:53,750
What?

1103
00:41:53,750 --> 00:41:55,720
But can you come up...

1104
00:41:55,720 --> 00:41:57,990
with so many highlights?

1105
00:41:58,150 --> 00:41:59,260
Of course I can.

1106
00:41:59,260 --> 00:42:00,690
I can make way more.

1107
00:42:02,220 --> 00:42:04,360
That's totally triggering her.

1108
00:42:04,460 --> 00:42:06,360
It was boiling up like crazy inside of me.

1109
00:42:06,460 --> 00:42:08,300
Both of them are fired up right now.

1110
00:42:08,330 --> 00:42:09,830
This is a full-on turf war.

1111
00:42:10,070 --> 00:42:12,500
I can make great choreography...

1112
00:42:12,500 --> 00:42:13,770
no matter the size of the space.

1113
00:42:13,770 --> 00:42:14,800
I can do everything.

1114
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:16,370
I have to show them what I'm capable of.

1115
00:42:16,510 --> 00:42:17,640
I'll take this battle on for real.

1116
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:19,140
My pride and career are on the line.

1117
00:42:19,140 --> 00:42:20,410
I can definitely win.

1118
00:42:20,410 --> 00:42:21,910
I will definitely do better.

1119
00:42:22,210 --> 00:42:26,020
Who will manage to defend their signature moves until the end?

1120
00:42:26,150 --> 00:42:28,550
Moving on, we will reveal the choreographers...

1121
00:42:28,550 --> 00:42:31,390
for the next 1-on-1 Signature Mission matchup.

1122
00:42:31,650 --> 00:42:32,720
(Nervous)

1123
00:42:32,720 --> 00:42:34,160
This isn't the time for me to be laughing.

1124
00:42:34,520 --> 00:42:35,890
I feel like it's going to be Koo Young.

1125
00:42:40,560 --> 00:42:41,600
(The choreographer for the second matchup: Back Koo Young)

1126
00:42:41,600 --> 00:42:43,970
- My goodness. - I knew it.

1127
00:42:44,030 --> 00:42:46,170
I need earplugs.

1128
00:42:46,170 --> 00:42:47,570
What had to come has finally arrived.

1129
00:42:47,570 --> 00:42:49,670
Actually, Koo Young is someone who could be here as a judge.

1130
00:42:49,740 --> 00:42:50,940
The Father of K-pop.

1131
00:42:50,970 --> 00:42:52,440
Back Koo Young as a choreographer?

1132
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:54,180
He is a legend.

1133
00:42:54,180 --> 00:42:55,680
INGYOO, what's with you?

1134
00:42:55,680 --> 00:42:56,880
(Giggling)

1135
00:42:56,880 --> 00:43:00,180
When it comes to directing, he's built up a monstrous amount of data.

1136
00:43:00,180 --> 00:43:01,650
He probably has the most data out of anyone.

1137
00:43:01,650 --> 00:43:04,050
(Back Koo Young's choreography and directing portfolio)

1138
00:43:04,050 --> 00:43:05,720
He has 24 years of experience.

1139
00:43:05,720 --> 00:43:07,660
That's more years than my age.

1140
00:43:07,660 --> 00:43:09,430
(24 years of career experience, 23 years of age)

1141
00:43:09,430 --> 00:43:11,960
I don't think anyone can disregard Koo Young's seasoned experience.

1142
00:43:11,960 --> 00:43:13,160
An unrivaled style.

1143
00:43:13,160 --> 00:43:14,860
- He's the one and only. - Right.

1144
00:43:14,860 --> 00:43:16,770
But honestly,

1145
00:43:18,270 --> 00:43:19,300
it feels like...

1146
00:43:19,300 --> 00:43:22,910
older-style moves show...

1147
00:43:22,910 --> 00:43:25,140
in Back Koo Young's work.

1148
00:43:25,140 --> 00:43:26,810
Since he's been doing this for so long anyway,

1149
00:43:26,810 --> 00:43:28,410
his vibe might not really align...

1150
00:43:28,410 --> 00:43:29,950
with what young people choreograph these days.

1151
00:43:29,950 --> 00:43:31,250
(Uncomfortable)

1152
00:43:31,380 --> 00:43:32,480
Darn it.

1153
00:43:32,680 --> 00:43:34,880
There are certain trends that young people talk about.

1154
00:43:34,880 --> 00:43:37,550
If we compete on trends,

1155
00:43:37,550 --> 00:43:39,890
I'm not sure if he can express that well.

1156
00:43:39,990 --> 00:43:40,990
My goodness.

1157
00:43:41,860 --> 00:43:43,230
Hang on.

1158
00:43:44,060 --> 00:43:45,190
I found that pretty absurd.

1159
00:43:45,290 --> 00:43:47,960
When I look back at...

1160
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:50,970
whether other choreographers showed anything fresh,

1161
00:43:50,970 --> 00:43:52,940
none of it matches what I've done.

1162
00:43:53,270 --> 00:43:55,600
Back Koo Young definitely has his own generation...

1163
00:43:55,600 --> 00:43:57,710
and signature style,

1164
00:43:57,710 --> 00:43:59,980
but there's a repetitive vibe to his choreography.

1165
00:44:00,880 --> 00:44:04,580
The expression feels a bit too serious and heavy.

1166
00:44:04,780 --> 00:44:07,720
It's tough and stiff.

1167
00:44:11,290 --> 00:44:12,690
(This is driving me crazy.)

1168
00:44:13,160 --> 00:44:15,290
But saying that just proves they haven't seen all my work...

1169
00:44:15,290 --> 00:44:17,030
and don't know who I am.

1170
00:44:17,390 --> 00:44:18,390
(Walking on eggshells)

1171
00:44:18,390 --> 00:44:21,430
I've seen a lot of his past work,

1172
00:44:21,430 --> 00:44:24,200
but I can't really recall...

1173
00:44:24,200 --> 00:44:26,670
what he's worked on recently.

1174
00:44:26,770 --> 00:44:27,870
My goodness.

1175
00:44:28,900 --> 00:44:31,010
It seems NaiN has been running forward with tunnel vision,

1176
00:44:31,010 --> 00:44:33,410
unaware of what people around her are doing.

1177
00:44:33,410 --> 00:44:35,440
I'm not at a level where I need to brag...

1178
00:44:35,440 --> 00:44:38,080
about doing this and that right now.

1179
00:44:38,450 --> 00:44:40,080
It feels like TV appearances...

1180
00:44:40,080 --> 00:44:42,420
have become his main focus rather than creating choreography.

1181
00:44:42,420 --> 00:44:44,050
While some people keep...

1182
00:44:44,050 --> 00:44:46,360
dancing passionately even after appearing on TV,

1183
00:44:46,360 --> 00:44:49,160
others completely pivot toward the TV appearances.

1184
00:44:50,730 --> 00:44:51,830
Unbelievable.

1185
00:44:52,160 --> 00:44:53,560
Actually, most TV shows...

1186
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:56,030
invite me as a judge.

1187
00:44:56,030 --> 00:44:58,070
If just anyone could do it,

1188
00:44:58,070 --> 00:44:59,230
they would be the ones doing it.

1189
00:45:00,070 --> 00:45:02,870
I believe being a choreographer has its prime time.

1190
00:45:03,206 --> 00:45:05,276
It feels like his lifespan...

1191
00:45:05,276 --> 00:45:08,076
as a choreographer has...

1192
00:45:08,076 --> 00:45:10,246
somewhat run out.

1193
00:45:10,246 --> 00:45:12,116
(Shocked)

1194
00:45:12,316 --> 00:45:13,416
It has somewhat run out.

1195
00:45:14,416 --> 00:45:16,016
(Hang on.)

1196
00:45:16,016 --> 00:45:17,116
It's not like that.

1197
00:45:17,116 --> 00:45:19,926
This time it wasn't INGYOO, but BABYZOO, who was the sniper.

1198
00:45:20,856 --> 00:45:22,126
That's the most shocking part.

1199
00:45:22,426 --> 00:45:24,456
Is this a battle challenge?

1200
00:45:24,756 --> 00:45:26,296
Should I accept it?

1201
00:45:26,696 --> 00:45:29,936
So this is a battle of directing and choreographing.

1202
00:45:29,936 --> 00:45:32,466
I do wonder if he can balance...

1203
00:45:32,466 --> 00:45:34,236
both of those aspects properly.

1204
00:45:34,366 --> 00:45:37,536
When it comes to directing skills shown through dance,

1205
00:45:37,536 --> 00:45:40,576
I'm not sure if he can deliver versatile formations...

1206
00:45:40,576 --> 00:45:44,076
without relying on props or camera work.

1207
00:45:44,916 --> 00:45:45,916
Hey.

1208
00:45:46,586 --> 00:45:49,216
She's young, so she has such narrow vision.

1209
00:45:49,616 --> 00:45:51,616
Hang on.

1210
00:45:52,016 --> 00:45:53,956
Back Koo Young versus him?

1211
00:45:53,956 --> 00:45:55,886
This is going to be so much fun.

1212
00:45:55,886 --> 00:45:58,356
- The two of them have worked a lot. - Who was it?

1213
00:45:58,356 --> 00:45:59,696
I used to take him everywhere...

1214
00:45:59,696 --> 00:46:00,996
- like my personal keychain. - Really?

1215
00:46:00,996 --> 00:46:05,136
I want to see the two of them go head-to-head for once.

1216
00:46:06,606 --> 00:46:09,536
My goodness!

1217
00:46:09,836 --> 00:46:11,006
This is fun.

1218
00:46:11,176 --> 00:46:14,706
After all, they have worked together for a long time.

1219
00:46:14,706 --> 00:46:15,876
- Hello. - Hello.

1220
00:46:15,946 --> 00:46:17,516
(Choreographer Back Koo Young's right-hand man)

1221
00:46:17,516 --> 00:46:18,746
(Choreographer Kasper)

1222
00:46:18,876 --> 00:46:20,486
Back Koo Young's number one discovery.

1223
00:46:20,546 --> 00:46:22,146
Back in the day, I was his keychain guy.

1224
00:46:22,146 --> 00:46:23,556
(Voluntarily exposing his own past)

1225
00:46:23,686 --> 00:46:24,986
Kasper is also famous...

1226
00:46:24,986 --> 00:46:27,786
as a defining choreographer...

1227
00:46:27,786 --> 00:46:29,826
for SM Entertainment.

1228
00:46:29,826 --> 00:46:31,696
He's amazing, but...

1229
00:46:31,696 --> 00:46:33,696
When it comes to EXO, it's Back Koo Young.

1230
00:46:33,696 --> 00:46:34,766
(Shocked)

1231
00:46:34,766 --> 00:46:35,766
(Let me see.)

1232
00:46:35,766 --> 00:46:37,496
Koo Young was the main director,

1233
00:46:37,496 --> 00:46:40,836
and Kasper was the sub-director or choreographer.

1234
00:46:40,936 --> 00:46:42,336
When you think about whether the EXO members...

1235
00:46:42,336 --> 00:46:46,106
relied more on Kasper or Koo Young,

1236
00:46:46,106 --> 00:46:47,806
it was obviously Koo Young.

1237
00:46:47,876 --> 00:46:49,106
Please stop.

1238
00:46:49,106 --> 00:46:50,916
But then again, you can never discount experience.

1239
00:46:50,916 --> 00:46:52,276
He's experienced indeed.

1240
00:46:52,276 --> 00:46:54,946
But does Kasper have his signature moves?

1241
00:46:54,946 --> 00:46:56,246
Is there anything?

1242
00:46:56,556 --> 00:46:57,786
This is no joke.

1243
00:46:58,016 --> 00:47:00,726
After all, the artists he worked with weren't rookies...

1244
00:47:00,726 --> 00:47:03,996
but seasoned performers with tons of experience.

1245
00:47:03,996 --> 00:47:07,126
There isn't really anyone else other than them.

1246
00:47:08,366 --> 00:47:10,136
My goodness. How scary.

1247
00:47:10,336 --> 00:47:13,266
He might be weak when it comes to directing rookie idols.

1248
00:47:13,266 --> 00:47:14,336
My goodness.

1249
00:47:14,936 --> 00:47:18,006
I received tons of requests for current-generation idol...

1250
00:47:18,006 --> 00:47:20,446
choreography and dance challenges,

1251
00:47:20,446 --> 00:47:22,346
but I turned them down.

1252
00:47:22,346 --> 00:47:25,476
I was too busy pouring my energy into TAEMIN and BAEKHYUN.

1253
00:47:25,476 --> 00:47:28,346
We don't know how it will turn out if that's true.

1254
00:47:28,346 --> 00:47:29,986
But frankly speaking,

1255
00:47:29,986 --> 00:47:33,156
Kasper isn't a choreographer the scene is seeking after.

1256
00:47:33,156 --> 00:47:34,686
(Kasper isn't a choreographer the scene is seeking after.)

1257
00:47:34,886 --> 00:47:36,496
(Tilting his head)

1258
00:47:36,496 --> 00:47:38,096
Did I hear that wrong?

1259
00:47:38,226 --> 00:47:39,396
I'm so scared.

1260
00:47:39,626 --> 00:47:43,396
Calling him a choreographer who's sought after for lead tracks...

1261
00:47:43,396 --> 00:47:44,896
feels a bit of a stretch.

1262
00:47:46,366 --> 00:47:47,466
He only worked on B-side tracks.

1263
00:47:47,466 --> 00:47:50,506
The lead tracks like "Danger" by TAEMIN were done by Ian Eastwood.

1264
00:47:50,506 --> 00:47:52,176
"Move" was also done by Sugawara Koharu.

1265
00:47:52,176 --> 00:47:54,376
"Don't Call Me" by SHINee carries Kasper's signature color.

1266
00:47:54,376 --> 00:47:56,106
But it didn't become a massive hit.

1267
00:47:56,276 --> 00:47:57,276
This is serious.

1268
00:47:57,276 --> 00:47:58,476
I'm really scared.

1269
00:47:59,146 --> 00:48:01,186
He has skill,

1270
00:48:01,186 --> 00:48:03,616
identity, and a category of his own,

1271
00:48:03,616 --> 00:48:06,316
but there's a reason why he never became mainstream.

1272
00:48:08,186 --> 00:48:10,726
That's a really sensitive subject.

1273
00:48:11,196 --> 00:48:12,526
What do we do?

1274
00:48:12,796 --> 00:48:14,596
I wanted to escape that room.

1275
00:48:14,996 --> 00:48:16,396
Can I be honest with you?

1276
00:48:16,396 --> 00:48:19,136
I consider that kind of talk to be very arrogant.

1277
00:48:19,136 --> 00:48:22,536
That means he has far too narrow a perspective.

1278
00:48:22,706 --> 00:48:24,576
Choreography matters,

1279
00:48:24,576 --> 00:48:27,106
but this is a battle fought especially through directing.

1280
00:48:27,206 --> 00:48:29,146
Directing means looking at the big picture,

1281
00:48:29,146 --> 00:48:31,846
staging it, and commanding the whole work.

1282
00:48:31,846 --> 00:48:35,846
But it seems he knows very little about that aspect.

1283
00:48:35,846 --> 00:48:39,416
I think we should filter guys like that out.

1284
00:48:39,856 --> 00:48:42,926
I want to show him what a true director really is.

1285
00:48:43,856 --> 00:48:45,456
Back Koo Young versus Kasper.

1286
00:48:45,456 --> 00:48:47,166
It's a battle of brothers.

1287
00:48:47,166 --> 00:48:49,496
The two went through thick and thin together for years,

1288
00:48:49,496 --> 00:48:51,366
so they share many overlapping titles.

1289
00:48:51,366 --> 00:48:53,166
They have so much experience.

1290
00:48:53,166 --> 00:48:55,636
This is the matchup I looked forward to the most.

1291
00:48:55,706 --> 00:48:58,506
Since they know each other best,

1292
00:48:58,506 --> 00:49:01,476
this battle is bound to be even fiercer.

1293
00:49:01,476 --> 00:49:03,776
Now it's an unavoidable clash.

1294
00:49:03,776 --> 00:49:06,046
I'm not sure what it is, but I think...

1295
00:49:06,046 --> 00:49:08,546
everyone is more curious about what I'll bring to the table.

1296
00:49:08,546 --> 00:49:10,086
Whatever comes out,

1297
00:49:10,086 --> 00:49:11,516
I believe it's going to be great.

1298
00:49:11,986 --> 00:49:14,386
It is different from mere reckless confidence.

1299
00:49:14,386 --> 00:49:15,986
Because I have everything I've built up so far,

1300
00:49:15,986 --> 00:49:17,156
I want to prove it.

1301
00:49:17,326 --> 00:49:19,726
I'll craft something as fresh and distinct...

1302
00:49:19,726 --> 00:49:22,026
from the original choreography as possible...

1303
00:49:22,026 --> 00:49:23,536
and give it everything I've got.

1304
00:49:23,966 --> 00:49:26,606
Moving on, I will reveal the next matchup.

1305
00:49:26,736 --> 00:49:27,806
Who would it be?

1306
00:49:28,236 --> 00:49:29,406
(Nervous)

1307
00:49:29,736 --> 00:49:31,006
I'm so nervous.

1308
00:49:33,776 --> 00:49:35,006
It's finally happening.

1309
00:49:35,906 --> 00:49:37,846
(It's MIN JUN.)

1310
00:49:38,646 --> 00:49:40,016
(His mouth is drying up.)

1311
00:49:40,146 --> 00:49:42,586
He's here representing The Stories.

1312
00:49:42,786 --> 00:49:44,816
Coming from the competition scene,

1313
00:49:44,816 --> 00:49:47,756
he gave off a different vibe.

1314
00:49:47,786 --> 00:49:51,096
I'm looking forward to seeing what kind of potential he'll show.

1315
00:49:51,896 --> 00:49:55,126
I feel like the others probably paired me up with MIN JUN.

1316
00:49:55,226 --> 00:49:56,366
MIN JUN?

1317
00:49:57,096 --> 00:49:58,466
He should go against Hash.

1318
00:49:58,466 --> 00:50:01,466
They're crews that are always competing in tournaments.

1319
00:50:01,566 --> 00:50:04,136
They have so much experience in mega crew performances.

1320
00:50:04,736 --> 00:50:06,906
Competition teams should battle against each other.

1321
00:50:07,376 --> 00:50:09,746
Hash definitely has to face MIN JUN.

1322
00:50:09,746 --> 00:50:12,316
Let the competition crews clash to see who is number one.

1323
00:50:12,316 --> 00:50:13,846
It can't be helped, Hash.

1324
00:50:14,186 --> 00:50:15,186
I look forward to it.

1325
00:50:15,186 --> 00:50:17,716
It looks like this place will soon turn into a live competition arena.

1326
00:50:18,516 --> 00:50:19,786
Let's go!

1327
00:50:20,026 --> 00:50:21,556
The mega crew performances.

1328
00:50:21,856 --> 00:50:23,456
This is going to be fun.

1329
00:50:23,656 --> 00:50:25,726
I wanted to go up against Hash once.

1330
00:50:25,726 --> 00:50:27,096
Should we call it a rival match?

1331
00:50:27,266 --> 00:50:29,196
MIN JUN stands no chance against me.

1332
00:50:29,196 --> 00:50:31,736
MIN JUN is probably terrified of me.

1333
00:50:31,866 --> 00:50:34,036
The Stories is famous.

1334
00:50:34,266 --> 00:50:36,806
But MIN JUN is...

1335
00:50:36,936 --> 00:50:39,536
The Stories!

1336
00:50:39,536 --> 00:50:40,776
(The hidden hero behind the championship)

1337
00:50:40,906 --> 00:50:42,906
What?

1338
00:50:43,276 --> 00:50:44,776
(Flustered)

1339
00:50:45,346 --> 00:50:46,516
(Avoiding...)

1340
00:50:46,516 --> 00:50:47,686
(eye contact)

1341
00:50:47,786 --> 00:50:49,116
Who? JEONG MIN JUN?

1342
00:50:49,116 --> 00:50:50,656
I've never heard of him before.

1343
00:50:51,156 --> 00:50:52,256
(Surprised)

1344
00:50:52,586 --> 00:50:54,056
JEONG MIN JUN?

1345
00:50:54,486 --> 00:50:55,956
Why didn't they bring in Kalvin?

1346
00:50:56,126 --> 00:50:57,726
I'm starting to lose interest.

1347
00:50:58,056 --> 00:51:00,566
(The room turns cold from the barbed remarks.)

1348
00:51:01,166 --> 00:51:03,066
It hurt my pride.

1349
00:51:03,066 --> 00:51:04,636
So I'm not that famous.

1350
00:51:04,636 --> 00:51:07,266
I don't think he's a director.

1351
00:51:08,566 --> 00:51:10,706
I've never seen him direct a project.

1352
00:51:10,706 --> 00:51:13,776
The director of The Stories is Kalvin.

1353
00:51:13,906 --> 00:51:15,346
I'm the co-director of The Stories.

1354
00:51:15,346 --> 00:51:17,576
I am confident in directing large-scale crews.

1355
00:51:17,776 --> 00:51:19,146
Co-director?

1356
00:51:19,376 --> 00:51:20,386
(Smirking)

1357
00:51:21,546 --> 00:51:24,556
That's a position where anyone can be replaced at any moment.

1358
00:51:24,716 --> 00:51:25,856
(Shocked)

1359
00:51:26,156 --> 00:51:28,126
(Annoyed)

1360
00:51:28,256 --> 00:51:30,926
It felt like he's just an underdog that a TV show needs.

1361
00:51:30,996 --> 00:51:31,996
That's true.
(Glaring)

1362
00:51:34,226 --> 00:51:36,166
It just means he directed a small segment of it.

1363
00:51:36,166 --> 00:51:37,936
That makes him a choreographer,

1364
00:51:37,936 --> 00:51:39,096
not a director.

1365
00:51:39,166 --> 00:51:41,806
There are people who can't tell the difference...

1366
00:51:41,806 --> 00:51:43,836
between a segment choreographer and a director.

1367
00:51:43,836 --> 00:51:46,806
That's not a director, buddy.

1368
00:51:47,946 --> 00:51:50,216
(That's not a director, buddy.)

1369
00:51:51,476 --> 00:51:52,976
(On pins and needles)

1370
00:51:54,046 --> 00:51:55,716
(Sighing)

1371
00:51:55,716 --> 00:51:57,156
Then what does being a director even mean?

1372
00:52:00,356 --> 00:52:02,186
I've already earned recognition at world-class competitions.

1373
00:52:02,786 --> 00:52:04,256
It felt like they were looking down on me,

1374
00:52:04,256 --> 00:52:05,456
so I was annoyed.

1375
00:52:05,856 --> 00:52:08,626
Not being recognized as a director right from the start...

1376
00:52:08,626 --> 00:52:10,436
could feel offensive.

1377
00:52:10,666 --> 00:52:12,736
He might have directing skills.

1378
00:52:13,296 --> 00:52:14,666
Still, he stands no chance against me.

1379
00:52:17,476 --> 00:52:18,476
(COME HERE, the powerhouse of offline competitions)

1380
00:52:18,476 --> 00:52:20,276
Hash is coming up.

1381
00:52:20,276 --> 00:52:22,146
I love Hash so much.

1382
00:52:22,146 --> 00:52:23,146
I love her.

1383
00:52:23,146 --> 00:52:24,376
Right after watching COME HERE's performance,

1384
00:52:24,376 --> 00:52:26,246
I followed Hash on social media.

1385
00:52:26,276 --> 00:52:27,286
(Pretty impressive)

1386
00:52:27,286 --> 00:52:28,386
She's so popular.

1387
00:52:28,386 --> 00:52:29,516
I love to hear the compliments.

1388
00:52:29,846 --> 00:52:32,016
When the music needs an explosive climax...

1389
00:52:32,016 --> 00:52:33,156
"My goodness!"

1390
00:52:33,156 --> 00:52:34,426
"How on earth does she pull it off like this?"

1391
00:52:34,426 --> 00:52:37,996
"How can she create such a breathtaking spectacle?"

1392
00:52:38,256 --> 00:52:39,426
She's on a different level.

1393
00:52:39,426 --> 00:52:40,426
It's unbelievable.

1394
00:52:40,426 --> 00:52:41,966
It's even more insane in person.

1395
00:52:42,996 --> 00:52:45,166
I always look up to her with pure admiration.

1396
00:52:45,166 --> 00:52:46,396
That's a mega crew performance.

1397
00:52:47,106 --> 00:52:49,866
They showered her with much praise, so I felt small.

1398
00:52:50,276 --> 00:52:52,036
Anyone would be surprised.

1399
00:52:52,036 --> 00:52:54,076
When it comes to running the mega crew,

1400
00:52:54,076 --> 00:52:55,976
I have nothing to say.

1401
00:52:55,976 --> 00:52:57,846
I believe she's a great director.

1402
00:52:58,176 --> 00:53:00,346
He recognizes my talent.

1403
00:53:00,346 --> 00:53:01,346
It makes me proud.

1404
00:53:01,346 --> 00:53:03,116
Hash is good, but...

1405
00:53:03,456 --> 00:53:04,556
She's good,

1406
00:53:04,556 --> 00:53:06,956
but does her work have enough charm?

1407
00:53:09,726 --> 00:53:11,056
It started again.

1408
00:53:11,756 --> 00:53:13,466
There's a performance made for a competition.

1409
00:53:13,466 --> 00:53:15,696
Dancers are perfect. Composition is perfect.

1410
00:53:15,696 --> 00:53:18,366
But just 1 thing. It lacks that 1 last thing.

1411
00:53:18,396 --> 00:53:20,106
It's a criticism I won't accept.

1412
00:53:20,106 --> 00:53:22,736
Perhaps she hasn't paid attention to my performance.

1413
00:53:22,736 --> 00:53:25,076
If my performance doesn't have the charm,

1414
00:53:25,176 --> 00:53:27,646
I don't know what performance does.

1415
00:53:28,146 --> 00:53:30,616
I'm not sure if she is able to come up with the moves...

1416
00:53:30,616 --> 00:53:32,876
that are fun and easy to follow.

1417
00:53:33,546 --> 00:53:36,616
The point that makes people amazed is quite different.

1418
00:53:36,616 --> 00:53:38,316
Her dances aren't for everyone.

1419
00:53:38,486 --> 00:53:40,226
(Her dances aren't for everyone.)

1420
00:53:40,556 --> 00:53:42,486
(Getting upset)

1421
00:53:43,496 --> 00:53:45,596
That must bother her a ton.

1422
00:53:45,956 --> 00:53:47,896
People won't watch if it's boring.

1423
00:53:47,896 --> 00:53:49,266
They won't watch if the dance doesn't have the charm.

1424
00:53:49,626 --> 00:53:51,866
I think her performance lacked that.

1425
00:53:52,766 --> 00:53:55,166
We do a lot of difficult moves.

1426
00:53:55,336 --> 00:53:58,236
We haven't been crowd-pleasing,

1427
00:53:58,276 --> 00:54:00,146
but we're here to break that.

1428
00:54:00,546 --> 00:54:02,446
Making the crowd understand her dance...

1429
00:54:02,446 --> 00:54:05,016
would be the key to this match.

1430
00:54:05,776 --> 00:54:06,886
This is hard.

1431
00:54:07,816 --> 00:54:08,916
MIN JUN versus Hash?

1432
00:54:08,916 --> 00:54:10,656
Wouldn't I win?

1433
00:54:11,056 --> 00:54:12,456
I must win.

1434
00:54:12,556 --> 00:54:13,926
Goodness.

1435
00:54:13,956 --> 00:54:14,986
(It's fun to watch.)

1436
00:54:15,386 --> 00:54:16,826
They're on fire.

1437
00:54:16,996 --> 00:54:18,226
Hash is someone...

1438
00:54:18,426 --> 00:54:20,096
I must beat.

1439
00:54:20,096 --> 00:54:21,566
I joined this competition to beat her.

1440
00:54:21,796 --> 00:54:23,636
You've got some nerve.

1441
00:54:23,966 --> 00:54:26,396
Compared to the young co-director,

1442
00:54:26,396 --> 00:54:28,636
the original director,

1443
00:54:28,836 --> 00:54:30,706
the one with experience would do far better.

1444
00:54:30,936 --> 00:54:32,576
Hash will crush it.

1445
00:54:32,576 --> 00:54:34,676
If we compare The Stories and COME HERE,

1446
00:54:34,676 --> 00:54:36,176
they are both very strong.

1447
00:54:36,176 --> 00:54:37,546
But this is the directors' war.

1448
00:54:37,616 --> 00:54:39,576
I think MIN JUN will get completely crushed.

1449
00:54:39,846 --> 00:54:42,616
He will learn a lot through it.

1450
00:54:43,316 --> 00:54:44,516
My goodness.

1451
00:54:44,516 --> 00:54:45,856
I think he will be the first to go home.

1452
00:54:45,856 --> 00:54:47,386
(I think he will be the first to go home.)

1453
00:54:47,726 --> 00:54:48,956
That's too harsh.

1454
00:54:49,156 --> 00:54:50,226
That's so mean.

1455
00:54:50,756 --> 00:54:52,226
(Bothered)

1456
00:54:52,356 --> 00:54:54,026
I saw it coming.

1457
00:54:54,026 --> 00:54:56,296
Has he ever proven himself...

1458
00:54:56,296 --> 00:54:57,696
as the director?

1459
00:54:58,596 --> 00:54:59,796
I'm just...

1460
00:55:00,306 --> 00:55:02,266
worried about MIN JUN.

1461
00:55:02,266 --> 00:55:04,876
So many people here are worried for him.

1462
00:55:05,676 --> 00:55:07,746
Look at his eyes.

1463
00:55:07,746 --> 00:55:08,906
(Fighting power up)

1464
00:55:09,076 --> 00:55:10,176
I'm scared.

1465
00:55:10,376 --> 00:55:11,916
Competing against Hash,

1466
00:55:11,916 --> 00:55:13,786
in a way is my fate.

1467
00:55:13,986 --> 00:55:16,186
I won't avoid it. I will face it head-on.

1468
00:55:16,716 --> 00:55:18,816
Look at that spirit.

1469
00:55:18,816 --> 00:55:20,826
They are on fire.

1470
00:55:20,826 --> 00:55:22,126
Unbelievable.

1471
00:55:22,456 --> 00:55:24,456
He's got some nerve to say that.

1472
00:55:24,456 --> 00:55:26,596
I've been with The Stories for seven years.

1473
00:55:26,596 --> 00:55:28,826
I strongly believe the data I've accumulated...

1474
00:55:28,826 --> 00:55:30,736
through those years is not to be taken lightly.

1475
00:55:30,736 --> 00:55:33,166
I will prove to everyone what it took me...

1476
00:55:33,166 --> 00:55:35,506
to join this competition. The underdog will strike back.

1477
00:55:36,306 --> 00:55:38,106
Do we have two left now?

1478
00:55:38,106 --> 00:55:39,236
It's about time it's revealed.

1479
00:55:39,236 --> 00:55:40,246
It's killing me.

1480
00:55:40,246 --> 00:55:41,346
Who is it?

1481
00:55:41,346 --> 00:55:42,376
I think it's BABYZOO.

1482
00:55:42,776 --> 00:55:44,546
- Who? - BABYZOO.

1483
00:55:48,446 --> 00:55:49,516
BABYZOO.

1484
00:55:50,516 --> 00:55:51,516
Bam.

1485
00:55:51,516 --> 00:55:53,486
I thought, "Here it comes."

1486
00:55:53,486 --> 00:55:55,256
- BABYZOO. - I was scared.

1487
00:55:55,256 --> 00:55:57,726
I should stand strong because they rip me apart.

1488
00:55:58,526 --> 00:56:00,056
They just rip me apart.

1489
00:56:00,296 --> 00:56:02,426
This is cute. Are those paws?

1490
00:56:02,426 --> 00:56:04,066
- Because he's a "zoo." - Because he's a "zoo?"

1491
00:56:04,066 --> 00:56:05,136
(Roaring)

1492
00:56:05,136 --> 00:56:06,836
He's cute, you know.

1493
00:56:06,836 --> 00:56:08,706
But he's Mr. Ambitious.

1494
00:56:10,106 --> 00:56:11,706
He won the battle.

1495
00:56:11,706 --> 00:56:13,236
He began as a street dancer,

1496
00:56:13,236 --> 00:56:14,346
but he choreographed,

1497
00:56:14,346 --> 00:56:17,946
and he's got a lot of his own signature moves now.

1498
00:56:18,316 --> 00:56:19,716
Look at all those wins.

1499
00:56:19,716 --> 00:56:21,346
That's impossible to achieve.

1500
00:56:21,486 --> 00:56:22,586
He's happy.

1501
00:56:23,186 --> 00:56:25,586
I'm very proud of it.

1502
00:56:25,586 --> 00:56:26,926
He's good at battles,

1503
00:56:26,926 --> 00:56:28,056
and he's a good choreographer.

1504
00:56:28,126 --> 00:56:30,596
It's not easy to be accepted as a choreographer.

1505
00:56:30,596 --> 00:56:32,256
He's proven his grit.

1506
00:56:32,256 --> 00:56:34,296
He's someone who can achieve anything he puts his heart to.

1507
00:56:34,296 --> 00:56:35,326
Right.

1508
00:56:35,896 --> 00:56:37,436
(During the choreographer lineup reveal)

1509
00:56:37,436 --> 00:56:38,696
What?

1510
00:56:38,896 --> 00:56:40,466
He's so ambitious.

1511
00:56:40,906 --> 00:56:42,536
How can he be good at all those?

1512
00:56:42,866 --> 00:56:44,406
What can you achieve without such big ambition?

1513
00:56:44,406 --> 00:56:47,346
I have to go in thinking I can do everything well.

1514
00:56:47,446 --> 00:56:49,346
I think I can direct a mega crew well.

1515
00:56:49,446 --> 00:56:51,416
I've been directing for awards ceremonies.

1516
00:56:51,416 --> 00:56:53,146
Each time, I had to direct 30 to 40 people,

1517
00:56:53,276 --> 00:56:54,346
sometimes up to 80 people.

1518
00:56:54,446 --> 00:56:55,746
(His performance-directing of "2023 MAMA Awards")

1519
00:56:55,746 --> 00:56:57,086
(80 dancers in total)

1520
00:56:57,086 --> 00:56:58,886
(Hash)

1521
00:56:59,016 --> 00:57:00,986
(Well)

1522
00:57:01,256 --> 00:57:02,286
But...

1523
00:57:02,286 --> 00:57:04,556
the mega crew performances from the award ceremony...

1524
00:57:04,556 --> 00:57:06,556
of K-pop artists,

1525
00:57:06,556 --> 00:57:09,966
when compared to the other competition performances,

1526
00:57:09,966 --> 00:57:11,736
are far behind in skills.

1527
00:57:11,966 --> 00:57:14,436
What? What does he mean?

1528
00:57:14,606 --> 00:57:15,606
What?

1529
00:57:15,906 --> 00:57:17,576
It was shocking.

1530
00:57:17,706 --> 00:57:19,836
The more influential the artists are,

1531
00:57:19,836 --> 00:57:22,846
the more people will say their performance is amazing...

1532
00:57:22,846 --> 00:57:25,016
even if they just stand onstage and stare.

1533
00:57:25,076 --> 00:57:26,276
Directing mega crew performance for award ceremonies...

1534
00:57:26,276 --> 00:57:27,286
doesn't seem too difficult.

1535
00:57:27,286 --> 00:57:29,586
Because it's an artist's performance,

1536
00:57:29,586 --> 00:57:33,286
the dancers are just there to complete the picture.

1537
00:57:33,316 --> 00:57:35,456
They just go in and out constantly.

1538
00:57:35,456 --> 00:57:37,326
It's like a school talent show,

1539
00:57:37,326 --> 00:57:39,796
a heartless performance.

1540
00:57:40,126 --> 00:57:41,766
Isn't she too proud?

1541
00:57:42,026 --> 00:57:45,466
It seems she looks down on the K-pop scene.

1542
00:57:45,466 --> 00:57:46,636
She's mistaken.

1543
00:57:46,636 --> 00:57:48,236
She won't say that once she jumps into this field.

1544
00:57:48,236 --> 00:57:50,976
I hope she will get recognized for her talent...

1545
00:57:50,976 --> 00:57:53,036
and get a chance to work with such artists.

1546
00:57:53,276 --> 00:57:56,146
I will put on a mega performance only BABYZOO can pull off.

1547
00:57:56,146 --> 00:57:57,146
That's all it takes.

1548
00:57:57,146 --> 00:57:58,476
I can prove myself with that.

1549
00:57:58,846 --> 00:58:00,786
BABYZOO's opponent?

1550
00:58:00,786 --> 00:58:01,816
Perhaps NaiN?

1551
00:58:01,886 --> 00:58:04,156
I think it would be fun if he competes against NaiN.

1552
00:58:04,156 --> 00:58:05,756
BABYZOO and NaiN.

1553
00:58:05,756 --> 00:58:08,786
NaiN and BABYZOO.

1554
00:58:08,786 --> 00:58:11,796
They are both rising choreographers.

1555
00:58:11,796 --> 00:58:13,496
I think their dance styles are similar.

1556
00:58:13,496 --> 00:58:15,266
Powerful and energetic.

1557
00:58:15,266 --> 00:58:16,966
Sometimes masculine.

1558
00:58:16,966 --> 00:58:18,496
Sometimes very smooth, and the groove is on point.

1559
00:58:18,496 --> 00:58:19,766
Sometimes feminine.

1560
00:58:19,766 --> 00:58:23,006
I think they are people who can move back and forth between those styles.

1561
00:58:23,006 --> 00:58:26,276
And they always choreograph for the same artist.

1562
00:58:26,436 --> 00:58:28,546
They would choreograph for the same girl group...

1563
00:58:28,546 --> 00:58:30,716
and for the same boy group.

1564
00:58:30,716 --> 00:58:33,446
NaiN and BABYZOO. BABYZOO and NaiN.

1565
00:58:33,446 --> 00:58:35,016
They always worked on the same artists.

1566
00:58:35,016 --> 00:58:37,516
It would be fun to watch them go neck and neck.

1567
00:58:37,516 --> 00:58:40,056
Thinking like that, I'd like to see these two compete.

1568
00:58:43,286 --> 00:58:44,396
Okay.

1569
00:58:44,796 --> 00:58:46,326
(Competition is to be continued.)

1570
00:58:46,756 --> 00:58:48,896
I had a feeling we were going to compete again here.

1571
00:58:48,926 --> 00:58:49,926
(So fun)

1572
00:58:49,926 --> 00:58:51,236
It should be neck and neck.

1573
00:58:51,236 --> 00:58:53,596
The fight of the newbies who are both choreographers and directors.

1574
00:58:53,596 --> 00:58:56,706
For the past few years, they've been the popular choice of agencies.

1575
00:58:56,906 --> 00:58:58,006
Right.

1576
00:58:58,106 --> 00:58:59,736
Why are all the winners here?

1577
00:58:59,736 --> 00:59:01,446
Even after winning,

1578
00:59:01,446 --> 00:59:03,776
she's done a lot of other flashy gigs.

1579
00:59:03,916 --> 00:59:05,746
It's very rare to find a 24-year-old...

1580
00:59:05,746 --> 00:59:07,346
with such work experience in Korea.

1581
00:59:07,346 --> 00:59:09,146
She has seized opportunities at such an early age.

1582
00:59:09,146 --> 00:59:10,316
I envy her for that.

1583
00:59:10,516 --> 00:59:11,586
(The senior is envious of the juniors.)

1584
00:59:11,586 --> 00:59:12,986
I envy her too.

1585
00:59:13,056 --> 00:59:15,026
Envy is what I feel.

1586
00:59:15,026 --> 00:59:17,996
I think they are recognizing me.

1587
00:59:17,996 --> 00:59:19,026
It felt good.

1588
00:59:19,026 --> 00:59:20,966
She's very popular for her work on "Golden."

1589
00:59:21,596 --> 00:59:23,196
Does "Golden" have choreography?

1590
00:59:23,196 --> 00:59:25,496
(Does "Golden" have choreography?)

1591
00:59:25,736 --> 00:59:26,736
My gosh.

1592
00:59:26,736 --> 00:59:28,236
I am telling the truth.

1593
00:59:28,236 --> 00:59:29,466
Do you know?

1594
00:59:29,466 --> 00:59:30,676
Do you remember the dance?

1595
00:59:30,676 --> 00:59:33,236
I'm not so familiar with the choreography of "Golden."

1596
00:59:33,236 --> 00:59:34,376
I'm not sure.

1597
00:59:34,846 --> 00:59:36,346
I was so conscious of her.

1598
00:59:36,346 --> 00:59:37,876
It's always the three of them on stage,

1599
00:59:37,876 --> 00:59:39,946
singing "We going!"

1600
00:59:39,946 --> 00:59:41,286
(Laughing)

1601
00:59:41,346 --> 00:59:42,616
Singing live.

1602
00:59:44,686 --> 00:59:46,756
I was a little shocked.

1603
00:59:46,756 --> 00:59:50,386
It feels like she's riding on the movie's success.

1604
00:59:51,726 --> 00:59:54,566
It's a work of quality.

1605
00:59:54,966 --> 00:59:56,926
It's a piece that's been acclaimed by the world.

1606
00:59:56,926 --> 00:59:59,236
It's also the work that promoted K-pop choreography to the world.

1607
00:59:59,236 --> 01:00:01,266
I don't think it's something to be looked down.

1608
01:00:01,366 --> 01:00:04,206
But NaiN is...

1609
01:00:04,206 --> 01:00:07,846
not so good at highlights. They are not highlight-worthy.

1610
01:00:07,846 --> 01:00:10,446
There aren't many moves that are worth remembering.

1611
01:00:10,816 --> 01:00:13,946
I think her weakness is the highlights that stand out.

1612
01:00:14,086 --> 01:00:16,416
Her choreography lacks highlights. She says so too.

1613
01:00:16,416 --> 01:00:17,756
To be perfectly honest,

1614
01:00:17,756 --> 01:00:19,286
I am not so sure...

1615
01:00:19,286 --> 01:00:23,056
what her style really is. It's not very clear.

1616
01:00:23,056 --> 01:00:25,356
This is what I am aiming for.

1617
01:00:25,356 --> 01:00:27,796
I don't want to be defined by certain styles.

1618
01:00:27,796 --> 01:00:30,496
I want to become someone with a wide spectrum of styles.

1619
01:00:30,496 --> 01:00:32,236
In that sense, I'm confident.

1620
01:00:32,396 --> 01:00:35,766
NaiN has won "Street Dance Girls Fighter."

1621
01:00:35,766 --> 01:00:37,906
So she must know how to play a winning game.

1622
01:00:37,906 --> 01:00:40,436
BABYZOO has competed in many battles,

1623
01:00:40,436 --> 01:00:43,246
and I applaud his dance experience and his understanding of dance.

1624
01:00:43,246 --> 01:00:45,576
If we were to make bets on them,

1625
01:00:45,576 --> 01:00:48,086
it would be a game with escalating stakes.

1626
01:00:48,086 --> 01:00:50,416
These two must compete.

1627
01:00:52,056 --> 01:00:54,556
I was very worried coming here.

1628
01:00:54,556 --> 01:00:56,686
I am a lot more relaxed now.

1629
01:00:56,756 --> 01:00:58,126
I believe I can do very well.

1630
01:00:58,126 --> 01:01:00,896
My energy is higher, and that's the truth.

1631
01:01:00,896 --> 01:01:03,426
If NaiN and I dance together or if we take turns,

1632
01:01:03,426 --> 01:01:04,696
I will be able to snatch the signature move.

1633
01:01:04,696 --> 01:01:06,366
That way, people will only remember BABYZOO.

1634
01:01:06,466 --> 01:01:08,206
He's so full of confidence.

1635
01:01:08,206 --> 01:01:09,406
So full of it.

1636
01:01:09,406 --> 01:01:10,506
I have...

1637
01:01:10,506 --> 01:01:12,236
no intention of losing.

1638
01:01:12,236 --> 01:01:16,206
This is a good opportunity for me to beat him.

1639
01:01:16,346 --> 01:01:18,976
I came here ready to go all out.

1640
01:01:19,016 --> 01:01:21,986
If I put my mind to it, I might beat him, you know?

1641
01:01:22,186 --> 01:01:25,216
We will reveal the next matchup.

1642
01:01:26,656 --> 01:01:27,886
Two people remaining.

1643
01:01:27,886 --> 01:01:28,926
It’s an automatic matchup.

1644
01:01:30,456 --> 01:01:31,826
(Sticking his tongue out)

1645
01:01:31,826 --> 01:01:32,856
(I'll do the same.)

1646
01:01:32,856 --> 01:01:35,126
BADA versus INGYOO. That will be intense too.

1647
01:01:35,126 --> 01:01:36,266
It's going to be fun.

1648
01:01:36,396 --> 01:01:37,966
It's WE DEM BOYZ versus BEBE.

1649
01:01:37,966 --> 01:01:40,336
I think BEBE is the women's top crew,

1650
01:01:40,336 --> 01:01:42,106
and WE DEM BOYZ is the men's top crew.

1651
01:01:42,106 --> 01:01:44,376
They've done many shows together,

1652
01:01:44,376 --> 01:01:45,776
and they've worked together a lot.

1653
01:01:45,776 --> 01:01:47,606
I can't wait to see them fight.

1654
01:01:47,606 --> 01:01:50,246
It's a showdown between two choreographers who defined an era.

1655
01:01:50,246 --> 01:01:52,276
BADA and INGYOO.

1656
01:01:52,276 --> 01:01:54,016
I want to see BADA and INGYOO fight.

1657
01:01:54,386 --> 01:01:57,286
Competing against INGYOO would be a real fight.

1658
01:01:57,286 --> 01:01:59,216
When she sees me in front of her,

1659
01:01:59,216 --> 01:02:00,316
she would feel threatened.

1660
01:02:00,316 --> 01:02:02,756
Maybe I will compete with BADA.

1661
01:02:02,886 --> 01:02:03,886
I saw it coming.

1662
01:02:03,886 --> 01:02:05,796
It would be the most interesting if we matched.

1663
01:02:05,796 --> 01:02:07,726
I'm taller, so I will jump over him.

1664
01:02:07,726 --> 01:02:09,166
I'm shorter than her.

1665
01:02:09,166 --> 01:02:11,296
But who knows? Maybe I've got something bigger.

1666
01:02:14,106 --> 01:02:15,106
It's intense.
It's wild.

1667
01:02:16,266 --> 01:02:17,736
- Let's go. - Go.

1668
01:02:18,636 --> 01:02:20,976
(What did the other choreographer think of BADA as a director?)

1669
01:02:20,976 --> 01:02:23,746
I told you, BADA had to be here.

1670
01:02:23,846 --> 01:02:24,916
Right.

1671
01:02:24,916 --> 01:02:29,116
Winning "Street Woman Fighter" is a huge career leap.

1672
01:02:29,116 --> 01:02:30,416
It felt good.

1673
01:02:30,616 --> 01:02:32,216
Why is she back anyway?

1674
01:02:32,616 --> 01:02:34,056
Go take a break, will you?

1675
01:02:34,856 --> 01:02:37,556
As a player, nobody can measure up to her.

1676
01:02:37,556 --> 01:02:40,196
Seeing her dance alongside Kirsten,

1677
01:02:40,196 --> 01:02:43,696
I believe she's one of the world's top five players.

1678
01:02:43,826 --> 01:02:45,736
When I dance next to BADA,

1679
01:02:45,736 --> 01:02:47,906
my masculinity might disappear.

1680
01:02:47,906 --> 01:02:50,066
(He might lose his masculinity.)

1681
01:02:50,066 --> 01:02:52,206
As a player, she's a legend.

1682
01:02:52,206 --> 01:02:53,206
However,

1683
01:02:53,206 --> 01:02:54,776
this is not "Street Woman Fighter."

1684
01:02:54,776 --> 01:02:56,046
(Goodness)

1685
01:02:57,516 --> 01:02:59,016
(Smiling)

1686
01:02:59,016 --> 01:03:02,816
(But this isn't "Street Woman Fighter.")

1687
01:03:03,046 --> 01:03:06,156
She will be competing as a performance director.

1688
01:03:06,156 --> 01:03:08,326
She will need some strategies.

1689
01:03:08,526 --> 01:03:10,186
I was very confused.

1690
01:03:10,996 --> 01:03:12,856
Among dancers,

1691
01:03:12,856 --> 01:03:16,326
BADA is considered to be that case.

1692
01:03:17,266 --> 01:03:18,866
BADA? BADA is...

1693
01:03:18,866 --> 01:03:19,896
a choreographer,

1694
01:03:19,896 --> 01:03:20,966
not a director.

1695
01:03:20,966 --> 01:03:23,406
Everyone wants to do challenges with BADA.

1696
01:03:23,406 --> 01:03:25,906
People wouldn't want to go to her for composition and direction.

1697
01:03:27,076 --> 01:03:29,106
She looked unhappy.

1698
01:03:29,706 --> 01:03:32,616
I felt very bad and upset.

1699
01:03:33,146 --> 01:03:35,816
She hasn't proven anything yet, so they think she's not good enough.

1700
01:03:36,616 --> 01:03:38,686
The air was heavy.

1701
01:03:39,416 --> 01:03:41,586
She's more of a heroine...

1702
01:03:41,586 --> 01:03:42,856
than a director.

1703
01:03:43,126 --> 01:03:44,996
She has to admit the fact.

1704
01:03:45,126 --> 01:03:47,966
I was born with the talent.

1705
01:03:47,966 --> 01:03:50,496
Not everyone can become the heroine.

1706
01:03:50,496 --> 01:03:53,136
"Psycho" mega crew was a little disappointing.

1707
01:03:53,236 --> 01:03:56,636
There were too many simple expressions.

1708
01:03:56,966 --> 01:04:00,106
When she composed and created flows for a big crew,

1709
01:04:00,106 --> 01:04:02,306
it felt weak.

1710
01:04:02,606 --> 01:04:04,316
(The fault is with BADA, the director.)

1711
01:04:04,316 --> 01:04:06,646
(At the time, other crews criticized BADA's mega crew.)

1712
01:04:06,846 --> 01:04:08,386
What's BADA's strength?

1713
01:04:08,386 --> 01:04:10,116
Nothing I can think of.

1714
01:04:10,216 --> 01:04:12,486
She clearly lacks the ability...

1715
01:04:12,486 --> 01:04:14,256
to create a performance for a large crew.

1716
01:04:14,926 --> 01:04:18,256
I felt like I was denied of my ability as a director.

1717
01:04:18,396 --> 01:04:19,826
BADA as the director.

1718
01:04:21,626 --> 01:04:22,896
BADA as the director?

1719
01:04:24,196 --> 01:04:25,496
(Hesitating)

1720
01:04:25,496 --> 01:04:26,736
BADA as the director.

1721
01:04:27,036 --> 01:04:28,136
This is too intense.

1722
01:04:28,136 --> 01:04:30,776
There are people who I can't think of as directors.

1723
01:04:30,776 --> 01:04:33,436
Those are sorted as choreographers.

1724
01:04:33,436 --> 01:04:35,446
Those who can direct...

1725
01:04:35,446 --> 01:04:38,076
are trying to take down the fake ones.

1726
01:04:38,846 --> 01:04:41,316
Who are the real directors here then?

1727
01:04:41,716 --> 01:04:43,986
BADA must have never heard of such criticisms.

1728
01:04:43,986 --> 01:04:44,986
It went too far.

1729
01:04:44,986 --> 01:04:48,286
I believe BADA needs more experience.

1730
01:04:48,286 --> 01:04:49,656
She's no match for me.

1731
01:04:49,826 --> 01:04:51,426
This is the directors' war.

1732
01:04:51,426 --> 01:04:53,326
So INGYOO has the advantage.

1733
01:04:53,496 --> 01:04:55,766
I should really show them.

1734
01:04:55,766 --> 01:04:59,296
It's my turn to show what I have as a director, so watch me.

1735
01:04:59,396 --> 01:05:00,866
(What does other choreographers think of INGYOO as a director?)

1736
01:05:00,866 --> 01:05:03,306
Goodness, INGYOO the Child is back.

1737
01:05:03,306 --> 01:05:04,706
(The father and child reunite.)

1738
01:05:05,076 --> 01:05:06,576
He's a talented choreographer.

1739
01:05:06,576 --> 01:05:07,876
He's the best choreographer.

1740
01:05:07,876 --> 01:05:11,516
I think he's the best male choreographer out there.

1741
01:05:11,616 --> 01:05:14,586
Every move he creates is trendy.

1742
01:05:14,586 --> 01:05:16,216
His dances are trendy and unique.

1743
01:05:16,216 --> 01:05:17,716
INGYOO...

1744
01:05:17,716 --> 01:05:18,816
is the trendiest.

1745
01:05:19,686 --> 01:05:22,026
Trendy? Not so sure about trendy.

1746
01:05:22,226 --> 01:05:23,456
(Not so sure about trendy.)

1747
01:05:23,586 --> 01:05:24,596
So harsh.

1748
01:05:24,596 --> 01:05:27,096
INGYOO and Kasper are the real deal.

1749
01:05:28,266 --> 01:05:29,326
This?

1750
01:05:29,696 --> 01:05:31,696
He's mistaken.

1751
01:05:31,696 --> 01:05:35,636
He wants to believe that he's trendy.

1752
01:05:35,636 --> 01:05:37,906
But all of these moves...

1753
01:05:37,906 --> 01:05:39,506
are the ones that were...

1754
01:05:40,236 --> 01:05:43,376
once very popular in the States but are no longer used.

1755
01:05:43,376 --> 01:05:46,216
These are the moves I did about 8, 9 years ago.

1756
01:05:46,876 --> 01:05:48,416
But they become hits.

1757
01:05:48,416 --> 01:05:50,916
It didn't become mainstream for a reason, you know.

1758
01:05:50,916 --> 01:05:54,086
It's like buying an outfit at an outlet...

1759
01:05:54,086 --> 01:05:57,626
and pretending it's a new arrival.

1760
01:05:58,226 --> 01:05:59,756
So intense.

1761
01:06:00,296 --> 01:06:02,066
I'm not making it up.

1762
01:06:02,266 --> 01:06:03,826
Kasper no longer...

1763
01:06:03,826 --> 01:06:04,996
has that young energy, you know.

1764
01:06:05,266 --> 01:06:06,496
He's lost his touch.

1765
01:06:06,496 --> 01:06:07,666
Or perhaps he never had it.

1766
01:06:07,806 --> 01:06:09,206
No matter who choreographed it,

1767
01:06:09,206 --> 01:06:10,566
"like JENNIE" would've been a hit, you know.

1768
01:06:11,076 --> 01:06:12,376
If that's what you truly believe,

1769
01:06:12,376 --> 01:06:13,706
go make one of your own and put it out there.

1770
01:06:13,906 --> 01:06:16,176
“like JENNIE” has the Dougie in it too,

1771
01:06:16,276 --> 01:06:18,146
and this finger dance is basically...

1772
01:06:18,546 --> 01:06:20,276
a straight-up copy of Afro dance.

1773
01:06:20,716 --> 01:06:22,486
It's a dance style called Tobetsa.

1774
01:06:22,486 --> 01:06:25,186
Afro dance has its own established moves, and I used them.

1775
01:06:25,756 --> 01:06:27,386
It's a genre of dance, so talking like that...

1776
01:06:27,386 --> 01:06:28,986
means he doesn't know a thing.

1777
01:06:29,356 --> 01:06:31,626
His weakness is that other people pull off his dance moves better.

1778
01:06:31,826 --> 01:06:34,666
As a player, I'm not so sure about him.

1779
01:06:34,966 --> 01:06:36,126
(Oh, dear.)

1780
01:06:36,126 --> 01:06:37,426
Does he have the stage presence?

1781
01:06:37,896 --> 01:06:39,066
When he stands in the center?

1782
01:06:39,066 --> 01:06:41,436
He's got no character on stage.

1783
01:06:43,366 --> 01:06:44,436
It hurts.

1784
01:06:45,036 --> 01:06:47,436
As a player, I'm better.

1785
01:06:47,776 --> 01:06:49,106
It might hurt him to hear,

1786
01:06:49,106 --> 01:06:50,916
but INGYOO has weak physicals.

1787
01:06:50,916 --> 01:06:52,916
If he had gotten good physicals like Vata,

1788
01:06:53,816 --> 01:06:57,516
he might not have had the chance to direct at this early age.

1789
01:06:57,856 --> 01:06:59,116
I am aware of it,

1790
01:06:59,116 --> 01:07:01,886
and that is precisely why my directing skill is where it's at.

1791
01:07:01,986 --> 01:07:03,686
If I had gotten the physicals like BADA,

1792
01:07:04,426 --> 01:07:05,996
many things might have been easy.

1793
01:07:07,056 --> 01:07:09,566
Eat and direct. That's all I do.

1794
01:07:09,996 --> 01:07:11,496
He's a great director. I give him that.

1795
01:07:11,766 --> 01:07:14,036
Vata is a top tier player.

1796
01:07:14,036 --> 01:07:16,136
INGYOO is the strategist behind him.

1797
01:07:16,336 --> 01:07:18,276
That's what you need a director for.

1798
01:07:18,276 --> 01:07:20,236
Flow, story, costume, and camera angle.

1799
01:07:20,236 --> 01:07:21,846
He's a very smart guy.

1800
01:07:21,976 --> 01:07:25,546
INGYOO's sharp mind and directing skill.

1801
01:07:25,546 --> 01:07:27,016
I respect him for that.

1802
01:07:27,046 --> 01:07:28,716
I was never impressed...

1803
01:07:28,716 --> 01:07:31,086
by his award ceremony performances.

1804
01:07:31,716 --> 01:07:33,486
I was incredibly meticulous about how I staged...

1805
01:07:33,486 --> 01:07:35,756
the award ceremony scenes.

1806
01:07:35,856 --> 01:07:37,996
There were so many layers of detail built into it.

1807
01:07:37,996 --> 01:07:40,856
Choreography, dancer placement,

1808
01:07:40,856 --> 01:07:42,566
lighting, and visuals.

1809
01:07:42,566 --> 01:07:44,226
How can he come up with...

1810
01:07:44,226 --> 01:07:47,466
something that makes people go wild every time?

1811
01:07:47,536 --> 01:07:49,836
Directing is all about strategy.

1812
01:07:49,836 --> 01:07:52,206
I think he's a really clever person.

1813
01:07:52,206 --> 01:07:53,436
He's so good.

1814
01:07:53,636 --> 01:07:56,946
BADA is the best female player.

1815
01:07:56,946 --> 01:07:59,516
INGYOO is the best director.

1816
01:07:59,516 --> 01:08:02,486
When they compete physically, BADA would win.

1817
01:08:02,746 --> 01:08:04,286
She's taller,

1818
01:08:04,286 --> 01:08:05,986
and when she does big, powerful moves,

1819
01:08:05,986 --> 01:08:08,286
you can feel that energy.

1820
01:08:08,756 --> 01:08:11,196
I think INGYOO would be really good at the strategic side of it.

1821
01:08:11,696 --> 01:08:12,896
If I dance,

1822
01:08:12,896 --> 01:08:14,526
then I will win.

1823
01:08:15,566 --> 01:08:16,766
BADA?

1824
01:08:17,196 --> 01:08:18,766
Wouldn't she want my direction?

1825
01:08:19,696 --> 01:08:21,266
He's got so much confidence.

1826
01:08:21,436 --> 01:08:22,636
I'm confident about that.

1827
01:08:26,536 --> 01:08:28,376
(BADA and INGYOO are the last matchup.)

1828
01:08:29,106 --> 01:08:30,146
(An uneasy tension fills the square...)

1829
01:08:30,146 --> 01:08:32,746
(as the matchup video is revealed.)

1830
01:08:32,746 --> 01:08:34,716
The two choreographers who captured the hearts...

1831
01:08:34,716 --> 01:08:37,886
of both the industry and the public will be competing head-on.

1832
01:08:38,056 --> 01:08:39,816
This is wild.

1833
01:08:39,956 --> 01:08:41,026
It's going to be fun.

1834
01:08:41,386 --> 01:08:43,726
As you know, I’ve made it this far...

1835
01:08:43,726 --> 01:08:45,596
by finding ways to make up for what I lack.

1836
01:08:45,896 --> 01:08:48,266
So I think it’d be fun...

1837
01:08:49,466 --> 01:08:52,096
to show you why I earned the title of director.

1838
01:08:52,236 --> 01:08:56,306
While leading my small body, the reason why I've made it this far...

1839
01:08:56,306 --> 01:08:58,836
is my wild imagination...

1840
01:08:59,006 --> 01:09:01,776
and processes of turning them into reality.

1841
01:09:01,776 --> 01:09:03,606
That's what got me here.

1842
01:09:03,806 --> 01:09:05,016
So I should do a good job.

1843
01:09:05,476 --> 01:09:06,716
Well, first of all,

1844
01:09:07,686 --> 01:09:09,886
being on "Street Woman Fighter 2,"

1845
01:09:10,146 --> 01:09:11,916
I had never once lost my moves.

1846
01:09:12,086 --> 01:09:14,016
I protected them every single time.

1847
01:09:14,186 --> 01:09:17,226
That’s another weapon I have...

1848
01:09:17,226 --> 01:09:20,126
in my arsenal.

1849
01:09:20,256 --> 01:09:22,196
The directing mission hasn't begun yet.

1850
01:09:22,196 --> 01:09:24,636
So I thought I should show them and prove it to them...

1851
01:09:24,896 --> 01:09:28,306
why I am a good player.

1852
01:09:29,306 --> 01:09:32,636
All the matchups are revealed.

1853
01:09:32,636 --> 01:09:34,706
(Burning with passion)

1854
01:09:34,906 --> 01:09:36,076
It’s going to be a bloodbath.

1855
01:09:36,076 --> 01:09:38,876
Now, the signature choreography takeover match...

1856
01:09:39,146 --> 01:09:42,946
to claim the choreographer credit will begin.

1857
01:09:43,286 --> 01:09:45,856
The judging will be based on online public evaluation...

1858
01:09:45,916 --> 01:09:48,856
and evaluations by the choreographers.

1859
01:09:49,486 --> 01:09:50,686
Public evaluation.

1860
01:09:51,126 --> 01:09:54,026
First, the public evaluation will be conducted using...

1861
01:09:54,326 --> 01:09:56,996
short-form videos filmed after the choreography draft is shot.

1862
01:09:57,736 --> 01:09:58,936
For the public vote,

1863
01:09:58,936 --> 01:10:01,966
the choreographer whose video gets more likes...

1864
01:10:01,966 --> 01:10:04,676
from the show’s official channel...

1865
01:10:04,676 --> 01:10:07,336
will receive one point.

1866
01:10:07,846 --> 01:10:10,746
For the choreographers’ evaluation,

1867
01:10:11,216 --> 01:10:12,716
the eight choreographers will vote,

1868
01:10:12,876 --> 01:10:15,546
excluding the two in the matchup.

1869
01:10:15,886 --> 01:10:18,286
The final result will be determined...

1870
01:10:18,486 --> 01:10:20,686
by a total of nine votes. One from the public evaluation...

1871
01:10:21,056 --> 01:10:24,356
and eight from the choreographers’ evaluation.

1872
01:10:24,796 --> 01:10:28,066
If you fail to come up with a stronger signature,

1873
01:10:28,666 --> 01:10:31,466
you will lose your signature move.

1874
01:10:31,736 --> 01:10:33,036
- That's too cruel. - Now,

1875
01:10:33,396 --> 01:10:36,566
you will be given just two hours to create...

1876
01:10:37,736 --> 01:10:38,876
your signature choreography.

1877
01:10:39,436 --> 01:10:40,706
That's mad, isn't it?

1878
01:10:41,546 --> 01:10:42,906
- Two hours? - Two hours?

1879
01:10:43,706 --> 01:10:44,776
That's too harsh.

1880
01:10:45,446 --> 01:10:46,446
(Speechless)

1881
01:10:46,446 --> 01:10:47,616
Two hours?

1882
01:10:47,816 --> 01:10:49,586
(The new signature choreography challenge begins.)

1883
01:10:49,586 --> 01:10:50,946
Did the countdown begin?

1884
01:10:51,286 --> 01:10:52,286
Two hours?

1885
01:10:52,286 --> 01:10:54,186
This is all too sudden. I'm flustered.

1886
01:10:54,386 --> 01:10:55,456
I'll get changed.

1887
01:10:55,456 --> 01:10:56,556
I need to get changed first.

1888
01:10:56,556 --> 01:10:58,356
They gave us two hours, which is ridiculous.

1889
01:10:58,356 --> 01:10:59,796
(Simeez runs.)

1890
01:11:00,756 --> 01:11:01,766
Quickly...

1891
01:11:01,766 --> 01:11:02,826
(Losing it)

1892
01:11:02,826 --> 01:11:04,326
Two-hour time limit?

1893
01:11:04,796 --> 01:11:06,866
Take a top choreographer’s signature style...

1894
01:11:07,036 --> 01:11:09,136
and make it your own so no one thinks of them.

1895
01:11:09,136 --> 01:11:10,136
Do it in two hours.

1896
01:11:10,466 --> 01:11:12,576
It's a tough challenge for anyone.

1897
01:11:14,206 --> 01:11:15,206
Gosh.

1898
01:11:15,206 --> 01:11:17,046
Ten seconds have already passed. Hurry.

1899
01:11:18,276 --> 01:11:19,376
This is mad, isn't it?

1900
01:11:19,376 --> 01:11:21,586
Wait.

1901
01:11:21,586 --> 01:11:23,516
Take the heels off. I need to get changed first.

1902
01:11:24,446 --> 01:11:26,486
I have five minutes to get changed.

1903
01:11:26,486 --> 01:11:28,186
Wait.

1904
01:11:28,286 --> 01:11:30,026
This is too harsh. Wait.

1905
01:11:30,356 --> 01:11:32,356
The song. Give me the music.

1906
01:11:32,456 --> 01:11:33,826
How do I get the song?

1907
01:11:33,826 --> 01:11:34,926
Hurry.

1908
01:11:34,926 --> 01:11:36,626
Okay. I can do this.

1909
01:11:36,696 --> 01:11:38,396
Calm down.

1910
01:11:38,396 --> 01:11:39,736
I got this.

1911
01:11:39,966 --> 01:11:41,666
I wanted to stop the time.

1912
01:11:41,666 --> 01:11:42,936
Please.

1913
01:11:43,236 --> 01:11:45,576
So I have to choreograph "like JENNIE."

1914
01:11:45,806 --> 01:11:46,936
But how can I...

1915
01:11:46,936 --> 01:11:48,076
(BADA has to choreograph INGYOO's signature, "like JENNIE.")

1916
01:11:48,076 --> 01:11:49,106
How do I get rid of this?

1917
01:11:49,106 --> 01:11:50,106
I need to get rid of it.

1918
01:11:50,106 --> 01:11:53,016
I should protect my signature move,

1919
01:11:53,016 --> 01:11:55,246
and I need to steal another's signature move.

1920
01:11:55,346 --> 01:11:58,356
This is too difficult to be the first mission.

1921
01:11:58,516 --> 01:12:00,516
How about the music? I need the music.

1922
01:12:00,516 --> 01:12:02,556
(Everyone moves busily in chaos.)

1923
01:12:03,256 --> 01:12:04,526
(Calm)

1924
01:12:04,526 --> 01:12:06,126
(He's in another world, alone.)

1925
01:12:06,126 --> 01:12:08,666
Everyone looked confused.

1926
01:12:08,666 --> 01:12:10,326
I was a little excited.

1927
01:12:10,696 --> 01:12:12,636
I thought 2 hours was too much time to create a 30-second choreography.

1928
01:12:12,966 --> 01:12:15,066
There were glass walls,

1929
01:12:15,236 --> 01:12:16,866
so we had to look at each other.

1930
01:12:16,866 --> 01:12:18,636
I think they made these glass walls...

1931
01:12:18,636 --> 01:12:20,136
to make us feel the pressure.

1932
01:12:20,136 --> 01:12:21,306
I was bothered.

1933
01:12:21,376 --> 01:12:22,906
Wait. This is crazy.

1934
01:12:23,776 --> 01:12:26,116
I could see Renan in the next room,

1935
01:12:26,116 --> 01:12:27,676
and that really bothered me.

1936
01:12:28,286 --> 01:12:30,146
I can't stop seeing Renan.

1937
01:12:30,386 --> 01:12:32,956
The walls were all made of glass.

1938
01:12:32,956 --> 01:12:35,056
I didn't want to care, but I couldn't stop looking.

1939
01:12:35,056 --> 01:12:36,286
I couldn't stop taking peeks.

1940
01:12:36,356 --> 01:12:37,786
It bothered me greatly.

1941
01:12:39,296 --> 01:12:40,396
(Sighing)

1942
01:12:40,526 --> 01:12:43,196
A mirror blocked the view of NaiN,

1943
01:12:43,196 --> 01:12:44,766
and I couldn't see her at all.

1944
01:12:44,766 --> 01:12:45,896
(He's curious.)

1945
01:12:46,236 --> 01:12:49,136
I couldn't see what she was up to and how she was doing.

1946
01:12:49,936 --> 01:12:51,506
I thought BABYZOO would see me as a threat.

1947
01:12:51,506 --> 01:12:53,976
I didn't want him to look at me, so I turned the mirror...

1948
01:12:53,976 --> 01:12:56,776
to block his view before I started to work on my choreography.

1949
01:12:58,116 --> 01:13:00,476
She's on the opposite side.

1950
01:13:00,946 --> 01:13:02,386
Hash blocked the view.

1951
01:13:02,916 --> 01:13:04,186
I should block the view too.

1952
01:13:05,286 --> 01:13:06,916
I need to work on the choreography here,

1953
01:13:07,016 --> 01:13:08,756
but if the mirror is here, she can see me dance.

1954
01:13:08,756 --> 01:13:09,756
I wanted to keep it a secret.

1955
01:13:09,756 --> 01:13:11,526
You saw her as a threat.

1956
01:13:11,726 --> 01:13:13,956
She's my rival, of course I felt threatened.

1957
01:13:14,256 --> 01:13:16,166
He seemed to see me as a threat.

1958
01:13:16,226 --> 01:13:17,796
(I...)

1959
01:13:17,796 --> 01:13:18,896
(Well.)

1960
01:13:18,896 --> 01:13:20,896
Two hours are enough.

1961
01:13:21,036 --> 01:13:22,406
I'm not choreographing one whole song.

1962
01:13:22,736 --> 01:13:24,466
Kasper's signature is "Guilty."

1963
01:13:24,466 --> 01:13:26,906
Both the song and choreography are very popular,

1964
01:13:26,906 --> 01:13:28,046
but putting that aside,

1965
01:13:28,046 --> 01:13:30,206
I was confident because it was "Guilty."

1966
01:13:31,316 --> 01:13:32,316
I got this.

1967
01:13:32,316 --> 01:13:33,846
(Koo Young has to choreograph Kasper's signature song, "Guilty.")

1968
01:13:34,576 --> 01:13:36,316
I can see Koo Young over there,

1969
01:13:36,316 --> 01:13:38,356
tying his wrists and all.

1970
01:13:38,816 --> 01:13:40,056
I'm really stuck right now.

1971
01:13:40,856 --> 01:13:41,986
Why is it so hard?

1972
01:13:41,986 --> 01:13:44,656
I think the pressure I felt made it really difficult.

1973
01:13:44,656 --> 01:13:47,426
I needed a strategy to steal the signature.

1974
01:13:47,426 --> 01:13:48,866
I should do this here,

1975
01:13:48,866 --> 01:13:50,326
and I should do this there.

1976
01:13:50,326 --> 01:13:52,666
I think I was mapping out how it would unfold.

1977
01:13:53,536 --> 01:13:55,406
No, time, don't go!

1978
01:13:55,406 --> 01:13:56,606
I got this.

1979
01:13:57,706 --> 01:13:59,606
I had to steal the choreography,

1980
01:13:59,606 --> 01:14:02,006
but I wanted to steal the whole performance.

1981
01:14:03,276 --> 01:14:04,976
I thought I should stay really sharp...

1982
01:14:04,976 --> 01:14:07,846
not to lose "Love Shot."

1983
01:14:08,246 --> 01:14:10,716
I am confident about my "Guilty."

1984
01:14:10,846 --> 01:14:12,756
Choreography is what I've been doing, so I'm confident.

1985
01:14:13,416 --> 01:14:15,026
I have never lost "Smoke..."

1986
01:14:15,026 --> 01:14:17,086
to anyone.

1987
01:14:17,086 --> 01:14:19,896
I choreographed and practiced...

1988
01:14:20,026 --> 01:14:21,866
harder than ever not to lose it.

1989
01:14:22,226 --> 01:14:23,766
I can turn another's signature into my own.

1990
01:14:23,766 --> 01:14:25,036
I will pour my heart into it...

1991
01:14:25,036 --> 01:14:27,036
and steal the choreography of "like JENNIE."

1992
01:14:27,036 --> 01:14:28,266
I can't lose it to him.

1993
01:14:28,666 --> 01:14:30,366
I wanted to practice mine,

1994
01:14:30,766 --> 01:14:32,236
and I knew I could do a great job.

1995
01:14:32,436 --> 01:14:34,676
"Iron" is a good song to steal.

1996
01:14:34,806 --> 01:14:38,216
I'm very confident about creating a performance.

1997
01:14:38,576 --> 01:14:40,076
I thought I could steal it.

1998
01:14:40,416 --> 01:14:41,916
- Are you confident? - I don't lack the confidence.

1999
01:14:41,916 --> 01:14:43,116
I don't have the confidence to lose.

2000
01:14:43,116 --> 01:14:44,416
(Now they have less than 10 seconds.)

2001
01:14:45,086 --> 01:14:47,556
Five, four, three.

2002
01:14:50,126 --> 01:14:51,126
Zero.

2003
01:14:51,696 --> 01:14:53,856
Time's up.

2004
01:14:54,326 --> 01:14:55,796
(First mission, 1-on-1 Signature Mission)

2005
01:14:55,896 --> 01:14:57,196
(I will kill them all.)

2006
01:14:57,196 --> 01:14:58,766
(She's very aggressive.)

2007
01:14:58,766 --> 01:15:00,466
(It was hard to watch.)

2008
01:15:00,466 --> 01:15:02,536
(I wanted to hide.)

2009
01:15:02,536 --> 01:15:04,666
(BADA versus INGYOO is the big match.)

2010
01:15:04,836 --> 01:15:05,836
(I will steal it.)

2011
01:15:05,836 --> 01:15:07,436
(I think that choreography should not be chosen.)

2012
01:15:07,436 --> 01:15:09,146
(When there's the public evaluation,)

2013
01:15:09,146 --> 01:15:10,146
(nobody can beat me.)

2014
01:15:10,146 --> 01:15:12,746
(The public might not choose me,)

2015
01:15:12,746 --> 01:15:14,316
(but the directors will...)

2016
01:15:14,316 --> 01:15:15,886
(It felt repetitive.)

2017
01:15:15,886 --> 01:15:17,546
(It would've been nice if you had relaxed a little too.)

2018
01:15:17,546 --> 01:15:20,016
(The choreographers criticize harshly.)

2019
01:15:20,186 --> 01:15:21,286
(Relaxed)

2020
01:15:21,286 --> 01:15:22,856
(INGYOO is incredible.)

2021
01:15:22,856 --> 01:15:23,856
(He never loses.)

2022
01:15:23,856 --> 01:15:25,656
(I voted for INGYOO yesterday.)

2023
01:15:25,656 --> 01:15:26,656
(I did too.)

2024
01:15:26,656 --> 01:15:28,026
(I voted for you.)

2025
01:15:28,126 --> 01:15:30,166
(Which choreographer's name will go onto the credit board?)

2026
01:15:30,166 --> 01:15:32,166
(It will continue shortly.)

2027
01:15:32,366 --> 01:15:35,436
Now, signature choreography takeover match begins.

2028
01:15:37,266 --> 01:15:39,006
I can't lose "Iron."

2029
01:15:39,006 --> 01:15:40,236
I will steal everything.

2030
01:15:40,236 --> 01:15:43,246
Losing it? I can't let that happen.

2031
01:15:43,646 --> 01:15:45,576
I came up with a solid choreography.

2032
01:15:45,576 --> 01:15:46,616
I can win.

2033
01:15:46,616 --> 01:15:49,046
I will take "Guilty."

2034
01:15:49,146 --> 01:15:51,956
I will steal "Armageddon," no matter what.

2035
01:15:51,956 --> 01:15:54,186
I will steal hers, while protecting "Armageddon."

2036
01:15:54,386 --> 01:15:56,986
I’m going to put my own spin on it.

2037
01:15:57,226 --> 01:15:59,356
I will give my everything and steal it.

2038
01:15:59,356 --> 01:16:01,666
I will never lose "Rude."

2039
01:16:01,726 --> 01:16:03,496
I’m confident I can make people forget the original choreography.

2040
01:16:03,496 --> 01:16:04,626
I am certain of it.

2041
01:16:04,626 --> 01:16:06,096
(Signature Choreography Takeover Match)

2042
01:16:06,266 --> 01:16:07,836
Signature Choreography Takeover Match.

2043
01:16:08,106 --> 01:16:09,366
Here's the first matchup.

2044
01:16:09,606 --> 01:16:12,476
It's the match between the two choreographers...

2045
01:16:12,536 --> 01:16:15,006
who have the strongest presence...

2046
01:16:15,276 --> 01:16:17,046
in the current K-pop girl group performance scene.

2047
01:16:17,176 --> 01:16:18,716
It's Simeez versus Renan.

2048
01:16:18,716 --> 01:16:20,276
Oh, my gosh.

2049
01:16:20,946 --> 01:16:21,946
(Looking cautiously)

2050
01:16:21,946 --> 01:16:23,046
It's a legendary big match.

2051
01:16:23,346 --> 01:16:25,116
(A fierce showdown...)

2052
01:16:25,116 --> 01:16:26,656
(between two rivals kicks off.)

2053
01:16:26,656 --> 01:16:27,856
I was terrified.

2054
01:16:27,956 --> 01:16:31,226
They were so intense. Renan and Simeez.

2055
01:16:31,726 --> 01:16:32,856
Seriously, they were about to...

2056
01:16:33,496 --> 01:16:34,656
(Stops talking)

2057
01:16:34,826 --> 01:16:36,696
This is going to be a bloodbath.

2058
01:16:36,696 --> 01:16:37,696
I know.

2059
01:16:37,696 --> 01:16:39,366
They have the most tension between them...

2060
01:16:39,366 --> 01:16:41,866
out of all the 1-on-1 matchups.

2061
01:16:44,066 --> 01:16:45,076
(Peeking)

2062
01:16:45,076 --> 01:16:47,206
I choreographed it with the mindset of absolutely crushing everyone.

2063
01:16:47,806 --> 01:16:50,046
If you think you can crush me, go ahead and try.

2064
01:16:50,476 --> 01:16:52,776
I've never seen Simeez so worked up.

2065
01:16:53,046 --> 01:16:56,046
I worked hard to come all the way here.

2066
01:16:56,046 --> 01:16:59,586
I will have faith in myself and give my all.

2067
01:17:00,916 --> 01:17:03,086
Simeez is letting her fire out,

2068
01:17:03,086 --> 01:17:04,956
while Renan is keeping hers bottled up.

2069
01:17:05,156 --> 01:17:08,926
You could tell they came in with something to prove.

2070
01:17:08,926 --> 01:17:10,396
I didn't want to take part in their fight.

2071
01:17:11,296 --> 01:17:14,296
We once competed with "Whiplash."

2072
01:17:14,366 --> 01:17:16,936
Seventy percent of "Whiplash" was my choreography.

2073
01:17:17,006 --> 01:17:19,176
What comes to your mind when you think of "Whiplash?"

2074
01:17:19,536 --> 01:17:21,436
(Sealed the deal with La Chica’s choreography)

2075
01:17:22,776 --> 01:17:25,216
I was genuinely getting angry.

2076
01:17:25,216 --> 01:17:26,576
But can you come up...

2077
01:17:26,576 --> 01:17:28,746
with so many highlights?

2078
01:17:29,116 --> 01:17:30,416
Of course I can.

2079
01:17:31,556 --> 01:17:32,616
It was upsetting.

2080
01:17:32,616 --> 01:17:34,316
They both seemed pretty triggered.

2081
01:17:34,486 --> 01:17:37,726
There’s a really strong sense of rivalry between them.

2082
01:17:37,726 --> 01:17:39,956
They are eager to beat each other.

2083
01:17:40,926 --> 01:17:42,796
Just looking at their eyes, you could tell.

2084
01:17:42,796 --> 01:17:44,726
I didn't want to look anymore. I was terrified.

2085
01:17:45,396 --> 01:17:47,866
I thought I should retire if I lose.

2086
01:17:48,536 --> 01:17:50,236
That's how far I went.

2087
01:17:51,336 --> 01:17:54,906
This could seriously jeopardize my business.

2088
01:17:55,146 --> 01:17:56,706
I just need to prove myself.

2089
01:17:56,706 --> 01:17:58,416
I should do a really good job and win.

2090
01:17:58,816 --> 01:17:59,916
This is getting fun.

2091
01:18:00,016 --> 01:18:01,946
Simeez and Renan's match...

2092
01:18:02,446 --> 01:18:05,016
involves two great songs.

2093
01:18:05,116 --> 01:18:08,056
Renan's signature choreography Simeez has to steal is...

2094
01:18:08,156 --> 01:18:09,986
"Armageddon" by aespa.

2095
01:18:11,696 --> 01:18:14,826
Its choreography was such a huge hit.

2096
01:18:14,826 --> 01:18:16,296
There's not one person...

2097
01:18:16,296 --> 01:18:17,626
who doesn't know Renan's "Armageddon."

2098
01:18:17,626 --> 01:18:19,836
It's such a famous move.

2099
01:18:19,836 --> 01:18:22,106
You pop and slowly raise your hand.

2100
01:18:22,306 --> 01:18:23,506
(This is the highlight.)

2101
01:18:23,506 --> 01:18:26,636
The hand move of "Armageddon" was such a huge hit.

2102
01:18:26,776 --> 01:18:28,076
A choreographer who can create great highlights...

2103
01:18:28,076 --> 01:18:29,746
like Renan is very rare.

2104
01:18:29,746 --> 01:18:32,346
I gave my everything to "Armageddon."

2105
01:18:32,446 --> 01:18:35,086
I'm very proud of it.

2106
01:18:35,086 --> 01:18:36,716
It's impossible to create...

2107
01:18:36,716 --> 01:18:39,556
a choreography that's better than the original one.

2108
01:18:39,856 --> 01:18:42,586
I will make sure to steal "Armageddon."

2109
01:18:42,586 --> 01:18:45,396
It will be hard for Renan to make people forget my choreography.

2110
01:18:45,396 --> 01:18:48,366
Simeez's signature Renan has to steal is...

2111
01:18:48,496 --> 01:18:50,296
IVE's "BANG BANG."

2112
01:18:52,666 --> 01:18:55,466
Simeez's choreography of IVE's "BANG BANG..."

2113
01:18:55,466 --> 01:18:58,806
matches the song's energy well.

2114
01:18:58,976 --> 01:19:00,736
It's got both tension and energy.

2115
01:19:00,736 --> 01:19:02,576
I begin by hitting "bang" from the start.

2116
01:19:02,776 --> 01:19:04,646
It's the dance that makes you explode your energy.

2117
01:19:04,776 --> 01:19:07,676
Simeez is powerful and energetic.

2118
01:19:07,676 --> 01:19:09,846
That style suits this song well.

2119
01:19:09,846 --> 01:19:12,356
When you think that it couldn't get any better than this,

2120
01:19:12,356 --> 01:19:14,286
I choreographed it a little more.

2121
01:19:14,486 --> 01:19:16,926
I don't think any choreography would be as good as mine.

2122
01:19:17,056 --> 01:19:18,496
This is about coming up with a signature move.

2123
01:19:18,656 --> 01:19:22,066
The highlight is to create...

2124
01:19:22,066 --> 01:19:24,226
a memorable signature move for someone else's music.

